const e={U3000:["Control Module","U3000 is the catch-all for a fault inside the module that stores it; the attached failure-type byte says what kind. GM's front camera module uses :41 checksum, :42/:44 memory, :49 internal electronics and :51 not programmed, all without MIL, and then drops adaptive cruise.",["Weak or discharged battery leaving a stored internal-fault entry","Module software or calibration that needs an update or reprogramming","Real internal defect such as memory or processor failure in the module","Module running too hot, e.g. a windshield camera in strong sun"],["Warning or service message for the system run by the affected module","Assistance or comfort function switched off, e.g. adaptive cruise or lane keeping","Often no noticeable fault if the entry came from a one-off voltage dip"],3,0,["U3003","U3001","U3002","P0606","P0602"],"מודול בקרה"],U3001:["Control Module Improper Shutdown Performance","U3001 tells you that a module did not finish its orderly power-down: supply vanished or dipped before it had closed its tasks and saved its data, so it notes the abrupt end at the next start. Low voltage is the usual trigger.",["Discharged battery, battery swap or jump start cutting power mid-shutdown","Module software that logs the event too readily and needs an update","Loose feed, ground or fuse contact dropping out after key-off","Main or power-hold relay opening before the module is done"],["Stored code found during service, often with no complaint","Check engine light on and occasionally a no-start when the engine computer stores it","Missing steering assist right after start-up when the steering module stores it"],2,0,["U3012","U3003","U3000","P2610","P0685"],""],U3002:["Vehicle Identification Number","With U3002 a module reports that its own stored VIN is either blank or differs from the VIN that the rest of the car sends on the bus. GM's front camera module splits this into :51, memory still erased, and :56, any digit not matching the broadcast VIN; both run at start-up in Run with 9–16 V and do not light the MIL.",["Used module or lamp from another vehicle still holding its old VIN","New module fitted without writing VIN and configuration","Programming session broken off, leaving the VIN memory blank"],["Stored code right after a module or lamp replacement","Driver assistance or the affected function disabled until the VIN is written"],2,0,["U3000","P0630","P0602"],""],U3003:["Battery Voltage","U3003 is logged when the supply a module measures at its own pins leaves the band it needs; the byte gives the direction: :16 too low, :17 too high, :1C out of range, :68 a logged event. GM's front camera module sets it below 9.0 V or above 16.0 V after 3 s in Run and then switches off adaptive cruise, without MIL.",["Low state of charge or aged 12 V battery","Alternator or DC/DC converter charging too little or too much","Voltage dip while cranking or restarting in start/stop mode","Corroded fuse, connector or ground in the feed to that module"],["Comfort or assistance function inoperative, e.g. power liftgate or adaptive cruise","Reduced steering assist message during cranking or after start-stop","The same code stored in several modules at once"],1,0,["P0562","P0563","P0560","U3006","U3000"],"מתח סוללה"],U3004:["Accessory Power Relay","U3004 concerns the relay, or electronic switch, that feeds the accessory (ACC) circuits once the car is in accessory or run mode. On GM trucks the body module reads the ignition inputs, decides the power mode and energises the matching relays itself. Mazda documents the code in the start stop unit as U3004:17, an ACC relay line above its threshold.",["Spilled liquid corroding a connector in the relay control or feed circuit","Aftermarket device on the diagnostic socket or accessory circuit feeding back voltage","Accessory relay sticking or its coil damaged","Fault in the module that drives the relay"],["Ignition or accessory mode cannot be switched off, radio stays on","Flat battery and no-start after the car has stood","Accessory functions dead in accessory mode"],2,0,["U3005","U300F","U300B","U3003"],"ממסר כוח אביזרים"],U3005:["Retained Accessory Power","U3005 relates to retained accessory power (RAP), which keeps radio, windows or sunroof alive for a while after the key is switched off. GM's truck manual explains the logic: the body module holds its internal RAP relay for about ten minutes after key-off, and ends RAP early when a door opens or battery voltage sinks below a calibrated limit; some modules get the RAP state as a bus message instead.",["RAP relay or output stage staying on or not switching on","Faulty door switch signal, so RAP is not ended on door opening","Body module or radio software handling the RAP state wrongly","Wiring fault or add-on device back-feeding the accessory circuit"],["Radio, windows or sunroof working long after key-off or not at all after key-off","High parasitic drain and flat battery"],2,0,["U3004","U300F","U3003","U3001"],""],U3006:["Control Module Input Power A Circuit/Open","Modules with heavy loads often take more than one battery feed, and U3006 says feed A is missing or open. Which pin is A depends on the maker. In one GM brake module (25OBDG04B) feed A means KL30_1, which supplies the pump motor: if it falls below 53.85 % of the second feed KL30_2 for 75 ms, a blown fuse or short to ground is assumed, Type B with MIL.",["Blown or loose fuse in the feed A path","Discharged 12 V battery pulling the feed below the check limit","Corroded terminal, loose pin or chafed wire on supply A","Internal power switch or board fault in the module"],["ABS, stability or parking brake warning lamps on","Function of the module limited or switched off","Check engine light on in some vehicles"],2,3,["U3007","U3013","U3014","U3018","U3003"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],U3007:["Control Module Input Power B Circuit/Open","U3007 is the partner code for the second battery feed, B. In GM's 25OBDG04B brake module B is KL30_2, the supply for the valve coils: the module compares it with KL30_1 and sets U3007 when it stays below 53.85 % of that value for 75 ms, and also when the switch for valve power reports less than half the supply voltage for 50 ms; Type B with MIL.",["Blown or poorly seated fuse feeding input B","Low battery voltage making feed B fail the comparison","Damaged wire or spread terminal on supply B","Valve power switch or internal supply path in the module faulty"],["ABS and stability control warnings, functions shut off","Check engine light on in some vehicles","Often stored together with U3006 when the battery is weak"],2,3,["U3006","U3013","U3014","U3018","U3019"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],U3008:["Control Module Ground A","Modules that switch large currents are often grounded through two separate wires, and U3008 marks the loss of ground A. GM's 19OBDG03B brake module measures the voltage on both grounds and forms (G1 − G2)/(G1 + G2); each wire should carry half the current, so a result above 0.9 for 200 ms means ground 1 is gone, Type A with MIL.",["Loose or poorly clamped ground eyelet at the body or frame","Corrosion or paint under the ground connection raising resistance","Broken or chafed ground wire A in the harness"],["Steering assist or brake system warning in the cluster","Reduced power steering assist or limited ABS function","Check engine light where the maker classes it as MIL-relevant"],2,3,["U3009","U3015","U3016","U3006"],"הארקת מודול בקרה‏ A"],U3009:["Control Module Ground B","U3009 is the counterpart for the second ground path, B. In the GM brake module of 19OBDG03B the same ratio test runs the other way round: if (G1 − G2)/(G1 + G2) drops below −0.9 for 200 ms, ground 2 is judged disconnected, Type A with MIL.",["Loose nut or stud at the ground B mounting point","Corroded contact face at the strut tower or body ground","Damaged ground wire B or crimp in the harness"],["Intermittent steering assist or brake warning messages","Heavier steering or reduced brake control while the fault is active"],2,3,["U3008","U3015","U3016","U3007"],"הארקת מודול בקרה‏ B"],U300A:["Ignition Switch","U300A is a module's complaint about the ignition switch as a whole: the position or key information it receives does not add up, so it cannot be sure whether the driver wants off, accessory, run or start. The failure-type byte narrows it down.",["Key travel hindered at the lock cylinder, e.g. by a displaced grommet or trim","Module software that flags the run-to-start transition as invalid","Worn or dirty contacts inside the ignition switch","Open, chafed or corroded hardwired ignition line or connector"],["Start or restart warning in the cluster, possibly a no-start","Stored code in a lamp or body module with no noticeable effect","Key turns stiffly or does not reach every position cleanly"],2,0,["U300D","U3010","U3011","P2533","U0140"],"מתג הצתה"],U300B:["Ignition Input Accessory/On/Start","Judging by its name, U300B concerns the ignition line that should carry voltage in Accessory, On and Start, i.e. in every key position except Off. A module sets it when the level on that wire contradicts the power mode it has been told or sees on its other inputs, for example live with the vehicle off, or dead while the bus reports run. No manufacturer documents U300B publicly.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the switched feed to this input","Input wire open, shorted or backfed from another circuit","Worn ignition switch contact for this position group","Body control module sending a wrong power mode on the bus"],["Functions on the accessory and run feed missing or behaving oddly","Affected module running in a fallback mode with a warning"],2,0,["U300F","U300D","U3022","U3004","U300A"],""],U300C:["Ignition Input Off/On/Start","U300C covers an ignition input that, going by the title, is meant to distinguish Off, On and Start rather than simply switching between live and dead. GM's 2012 light-duty truck wiring manual has exactly such a circuit, labelled Off/Run/Crank: unlike the plain accessory and run/crank feeds it takes separate states for key out or accessory, key in and off, run, and crank.",["Contact resistance in the ignition switch shifting the coded level","Corroded or loose pin at the switch or module connector","Input wire open or shorted to ground or voltage","Faulty input stage in the reading module"],["Vehicle does not switch power modes as expected, e.g. no start or no shutdown","Intermittent warnings that depend on key position or switch movement"],2,0,["U3011","U300D","U3010","U300A","P2533"],""],U300D:["Ignition Input On/Start","U300D concerns the line that should be live in On and Start only, which GM calls Run/Crank Ignition 1; in GM's 2012 truck wiring manual it is active in run and crank and inactive in off and accessory. A module sets the code when this line and the power mode on the bus disagree.",["Body control module keeping the run/crank relay energized after key-off","Run/crank relay sticking closed or failing to close","Blown fuse or open wire in the run/crank feed to the module","Backfeed from an aftermarket device tapped into the run/crank circuit"],["Battery repeatedly discharged after the car was parked","Service engine lamp at start-up with P2535 in other modules","Cluster or other modules staying awake with the ignition off"],2,0,["P2535","P2534","U300E","U3023","U300C"],""],U300E:["Ignition Input On","U300E deals with an ignition input that should be live only in On, without Start. Such run-only feeds exist because many loads are shed while the starter turns; GM's 2012 truck wiring manual, for instance, keeps its retained accessory power relay energized in all modes but two, crank and off-awake. If a module sees this run-only line high in Off or Accessory, or low while the network reports run, it stores U300E.",["Blown fuse or faulty run relay on the run-only feed","Input wire open, shorted or backfed","Module software misjudging the intended drop during cranking","Worn run contact in the ignition switch"],["Functions on the run-only feed dead with the engine running","Code logged right after each start with no other complaint"],2,0,["U300D","U3010","P2531","P2532","U3005"],""],U300F:["Ignition Input Accessory","U300F refers to the accessory input, the line that powers comfort loads such as audio or power windows when the key is in accessory. In GM's 2012 pickup wiring manual this accessory voltage circuit is active in accessory and run but switched off in crank and in both off positions.",["Accessory relay sticking closed or not pulling in","Blown accessory fuse or open feed wire","Worn accessory contact in the ignition switch","Aftermarket equipment backfeeding the accessory line"],["Radio, windows or sockets dead in accessory, or still on with the key out","Battery drained after parking when the feed stays live"],1,0,["U3004","U3005","U300B","U3022","U300E"],"אביזרי כניסת הצתה"],U3010:["Ignition Input Start","U3010 concerns the start or crank request input, which should be active only while the key or button is held in Start. A module sets it when it sees a start signal outside a valid crank event, or misses one although the network reports crank.",["Worn start contact or push-button in the ignition switch","Start request wire open or shorted to voltage","Module software misreading the run-to-start transition","Supply dip during cranking upsetting the input reading"],["Engine does not crank or cranks with a delay","Code stored at each start with no further complaint"],2,0,["U300D","U300A","U300E","P2533","P0615"],"התנעת כניסת הצתה"],U3011:["Ignition Input Off","U3011 relates to the input that tells a module the ignition is off, for instance a key-in or off-state line. The code is set when that input reports off while the network says the car is running, or fails to report off when every other source does.",["Faulty key-in or off-position contact in the switch","Off-state input wire open or shorted","Body control module reporting a wrong power mode","Faulty input stage in the reading module"],["Modules not going to sleep, battery drained after parking","Functions switching off briefly while driving"],2,0,["U300C","U3022","U300A","U3012","U3001"],""],U3012:["Control Module Improper Wake-up Performance","Some modules must wake themselves while the car is parked, for example to run engine-off tests or battery checks, and U3012 reports that this went wrong. Ford's 2023 diesel OBD summary describes the PCM monitor: the code sets if more than two wake-ups happen in the ten minutes before a scheduled alarm wake, or if a requested alarm wake is still missing ten minutes later.",["Module software handling timed wake-ups incorrectly","Another module or add-on keeping the network awake or waking it repeatedly","Battery disconnected or supply lost while a wake-up was pending","Fault in a hard-wired wake-up line or its connector"],["Check engine light on with no drivability concern","ABS or brake warning and soft pedal right after start-up when the brake module stores it"],2,1,["U3001","U301A","P06E4","P24EF","P2610"],""],U3013:["Control Module Input Power C Circuit/Open","U3013 extends the input power family to a third feed, C, and reports it as missing or open. It only exists on modules with at least three separately fused supplies, such as large body or brake units. No manufacturer documents U3013 publicly, and nothing defines which pin is C; that is up to each maker's wiring.",["Blown fuse in the feed C path","Pushed-out pin, corroded terminal or broken wire on supply C","Weak battery or voltage dip during cranking"],["Part of the functions of the affected module dead","Lost communication codes in other modules if the unit shuts down"],2,0,["U3014","U3006","U3007","U3019"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],U3014:["Control Module Input Power D Circuit/Open","U3014 is the fourth member of the input power series and means feed D of a module is absent or open. Four separate feeds are rare, so the code appears mainly on central body controllers or power distribution units with several power stages. As with U3013, no maker publishes a definition for it, and the letter only follows that module's pin plan.",["Blown fuse feeding input D","Loose terminal or damaged wire on supply D","Flat battery, then usually with further supply codes in other modules"],["Individual consumers or functions of the module not working","Often stored together with other input power codes after a battery problem"],2,0,["U3013","U3006","U3007","U3003"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ D — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],U3015:["Control Module Ground C","U3015 reports that the third ground path of a module, labelled C, is missing or no longer plausible. Three or four separate grounds are found mainly on units that drive heavy loads, such as brake, steering or power distribution modules, where control electronics and power stages return current through their own wires. No manufacturer documents U3015 publicly.",["Corroded or loose ground eyelet at the body or frame point","Chafed or broken ground wire between module and ground point","Spread or corroded ground pin in the module connector","Internal fault in the module's ground measurement"],["Warning lamp or message for the system run by the affected module","Function cut back or switched off, often depending on load or moisture","Stored together with other supply or ground codes of the same module"],2,2,["U3016","U3008","U3009","U3013"],"הארקת מודול בקרה‏ C"],U3016:["Control Module Ground D","U3016 closes the ground series and stands for a fourth return path, D, that the module considers open or out of line with its other grounds. Four grounds on one unit are rare, so before chasing the D pin it pays to check whether grounds A to C are logged as well; several ground codes at once point to a shared splice, the battery negative cable or a body-to-engine strap rather than to one wire.",["Poor shared ground, battery negative or engine-to-body strap","Corroded or loose eyelet at ground point D","Damaged ground pin or water in the module connector","Fault in the module's own ground monitoring"],["Warning or service message for the affected system","Several ground or supply codes logged at the same time","Intermittent loss of the module's function"],2,2,["U3015","U3008","U3009","U3014"],"הארקת מודול בקרה‏ D"],U3017:["Control Module Timer/Clock Performance","U3017 means a module distrusts its own time base: the clock or timer it counts with disagrees with what it expects, often time received from another unit over the network. In practice it is mostly a software matter. Ram's 6.7 L Cummins trucks list U3017 in a long series of ECM reflash bulletins from 2014 on (e.g.",["Module software that flags timing differences too readily; fixed by reprogramming","Time or key-off information from another module arriving late or implausible at start-up","Discharged 12 V battery after a long standstill","Real defect of the module's clock circuit"],["MIL on without any drivability complaint","Code appears some minutes after start and later goes inactive","Reappears after clearing until the module software is updated"],2,1,["P2610","P262B","U3001","U3012","U3000"],""],U3018:["Control Module Input Power Circuit A/B Correlation","Where a module has two separate battery feeds, U3018 says that feed A and feed B no longer agree. In GM's 2025 body control module tables (25OBDG04B, 25OBDG03B) the two measured voltages are compared while a battery is detected and the starter is not engaged; a gap above 4 V in 4 s of a 5 s window fails the test, Type B.",["Blown fuse on one of the two feeds, often from a short on a load circuit sharing it","High resistance or loose terminal in one feed wire","Weak battery causing uneven voltage drops between feeds","Faulty voltage measurement inside the module"],["Service engine soon lamp or system warning, depending on the module","Functions on the dead feed stop working, e.g. A/C blowing warm","Logged together with a low-voltage code for feed A or B"],2,3,["U3019","U3006","U3007","U3501","U3505"],"מעגל כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],U3019:["Control Module Input Power Circuit B/C Correlation","U3019 pairs the second and third supply of a module and reports that they drift apart. The one published use comes from GM's electric brake booster module in the 2016 and 2018 hybrid tables (16OBDG02, 18OBDG01). There, one voltage sensor watches the booster circuit supply and a second one the supply of the motor driver;",["Voltage loss on one feed from a corroded fuse, terminal or splice","Drift of the voltage divider or sensor inside the module","Motor driver supply sagging under load from a faulty booster motor stage"],["MIL and brake system warning on the first trip","Reduced or harder brake pedal assist","Often stored with input power low or high codes of the same module"],3,3,["U3018","U3007","U3013","U3505","U3509"],"מעגל כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B/C — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],U301A:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit A/Open","A wake-up circuit is a separate wire that rouses a sleeping module without bus traffic, for example when a charge cable is plugged in or another controller needs it. U301A reports that line A has lost continuity, so no valid signal reaches the input.",["Broken wake-up wire or pushed-out connector pin","Corroded or loose contact at the sending or receiving module","Sending module or charger not driving the wake-up output","Blown fuse in a supply-fed wake circuit"],["Module does not respond, other modules report lost communication","Charging or a function that needs the wake-up does not start"],2,0,["U301B","U301C","U301D","U301E","U3012"],""],U301B:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit A Low","U301B means wake-up line A sits below its expected level, typically because it touches ground or is pulled down by a faulty sender. What happens next depends on how the receiving chip works. NXP's CAN transceiver TJA1043, for example, wakes on a change of the WAKE pin in either direction once the new level has stayed stable for a short filter time, and its switching threshold lies a few volts below battery voltage…",["Wake-up wire chafed through and touching ground","Corrosion or moisture pulling the level down at a connector","Sending module output stuck low"],["Module stays asleep, function or charging unavailable","Lost-communication codes in other modules"],2,0,["U301A","U301C","U301F","U301D","U3012"],""],U301C:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit A High","U301C is the opposite of U301B: wake-up line A is stuck high, usually shorted to a battery-fed wire or held up by a sender that never releases it. The receiving module then gets a permanent wake request.",["Wake-up wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Sending module or charger holding the wake output on","Moisture bridging the wake pin to a neighbouring supply pin"],["12 V battery drained after the vehicle has been parked","Module or fan audible or active with the vehicle switched off"],2,0,["U301A","U301B","U3020","U301D","U3012"],""],U301D:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit A Performance","U301D says wake-up line A is electrically intact but its level does not fit what the module expects at that moment. Ford uses it in the battery energy control module of the 2019 Fusion Energi plug-in hybrid.",["BECM and PCM software judging the wake-up timing too strictly","On-board charger raising its wake-up signal late or unsteadily","High resistance in the charge wake-up wire or connector"],["MIL on after a charging session","Code is the only entry in the battery control module"],4,1,["U301A","U3021","P06E4","P0E64","U3012"],""],U301E:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit B/Open","U301E is the open-circuit code for a second wake-up line, B, on modules that can be roused by more than one source, for example by a door or key event and separately by a charge or timer signal. Ford's patent US5945745A explains why such paths exist at all: a module may sit in a low-current state with the ignition off and still has to answer certain demands, such as panel lighting when the headlamps are switched on.",["Broken wake-up wire B or loose pin","Fault at a splice or sender shared with line A","Source wired to line B not driving its output"],["One wake-dependent function, e.g. timed or remote action, does not start","Module otherwise works normally once awake"],2,0,["U301F","U3020","U3021","U301A","U3012"],""],U301F:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit B Low","U301F reports wake-up line B held below its valid level, most often by a short to ground. Since B is a second, independent wake path, the module can still be roused through line A or the network; what it loses is the wake source wired to B.",["Wake-up wire B chafed and touching ground","Moisture or corrosion pulling line B down","Source on line B with its output stuck low"],["Function tied to wake source B unavailable","No other complaint while the module is awake"],2,0,["U301E","U3020","U301B","U3021"],""],U3020:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit B High","U3020 sets when wake-up line B stays above its valid level, typically through contact with a battery or ignition feed, or because its source holds it on. The practical effect differs from U301F: a permanently active B line keeps asking the module to stay awake even when line A and the bus have gone quiet, so the module cannot enter sleep and the 12 V battery runs down while parked.",["Wake-up wire B shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Source on line B holding its output on","Moisture bridging line B to a supply pin"],["12 V battery flat after parking","Module stays awake with the vehicle locked"],2,0,["U301E","U301F","U301C","U3021","U3012"],""],U3021:["Control Module Wake-up Circuit B Performance","U3021 is the plausibility code for wake-up line B: the wire is neither open nor shorted, but the wake signal arrives at the wrong time or does not match what other inputs say. No manufacturer documents U3021 publicly.",["Software in sender or receiver judging the wake timing wrongly","Source on line B raising or dropping its signal late","Contact resistance on line B slowing the level change"],["Warning lamp or message after a wake event, e.g. after charging","Function works, but the code returns sporadically"],4,0,["U301D","U301E","U301F","U3020","P06E4"],""],U3022:["Ignition Input Accessory/Off","U3022 is the last of the ignition input codes and, by its name, covers a line or line state that belongs to Accessory and Off together, i.e. to all positions in which the engine is not meant to run. GM's 2012 pickup wiring manual has a comparable case: its coded Off/Run/Crank circuit shows one common state for key out and for accessory, separate from key in, run and crank.",["Contact resistance in the ignition switch giving an in-between level","Input wire open, shorted or backfed","Body control module broadcasting a wrong power mode"],["Accessory functions behaving wrongly for the key position","Stored together with other ignition input codes in the same module"],2,0,["U300F","U3011","U300C","U300B","U3004"],""],U3023:["Control Module Input Power Circuit A - Ignition Input On/Start Circuit Correlation","U3023 means a module sees clearly different voltages on its permanent battery feed A and its switched run/crank input while both should be live. GM's 2025 engine and transmission control modules (25OBDG04B, 25OBDG03B and others) run this check once a battery is detected, run/crank is active and the starter is not engaged: a difference above 3 V in 40 of 50 samples fails it, in some ECM variants 50 of 63.",["Module harness chafed against a bracket, interrupting feed or ignition wire","Faulty run/crank relay or fuse feeding the ignition input","Voltage drop on the battery feed from a loose terminal or corroded fuse","Faulty voltage sensing inside the module"],["MIL on, often with several other codes from the same module","Engine stalls or does not start","Transmission faults when the TCM stores it"],2,3,["U3024","U3006","U3018","U3501","U3010"],""],U3024:["Control Module Input Power Circuit B - Ignition Input On/Start Circuit Correlation","U3024 is the same plausibility test as U3023, but against the module's second battery feed, B: with the key in run or start, feed B and the switched ignition input should show about the same voltage, and a lasting gap points to a fault on one of the two paths. The code only makes sense on modules with two permanent feeds plus an ignition line. No manufacturer documents U3024 publicly.",["Blown fuse or damaged wire on battery feed B","Run/crank relay or ignition wire delivering too little voltage","Loose or corroded pin for feed B in the module connector","Faulty voltage sensing inside the module"],["Warning lamp or message, depending on the module","Loss of functions supplied through feed B"],2,0,["U3023","U3007","U3018","U3505","U3010"],""],U3025:["Control Module A Disable Circuit/Open","Safety-relevant systems often give a supervising controller a hard-wired line through which it can switch off another module or its power stage, independent of the bus. Bosch patent US6804564B2 describes a first control unit that de-energizes a faulty second unit over such an output line, and FCA patent US10676100B2 shows a hybrid where control processor, motor processor and a monitor each have their own shutoff…",["Broken disable wire or unplugged connector between the two modules","Corroded or pushed-out pin on the disable line","Output driver of the supervising module no longer driving the line","Input stage of module A misreading the line"],["Function of module A unavailable, e.g. drive system not ready","System warning message in the cluster"],3,2,["U3026","U3027","U3028","P2C96"],""],U3026:["Control Module A Disable Circuit Low","U3026 is logged when the disable line to module A sits below its valid voltage range, typically because it is shorted to ground. What that means depends on the polarity the maker chose. In the Siemens control unit of patent US7596436B2 the enable signal is high for run and low for shutdown, and a monitoring circuit cuts the output stages by pulling the shutdown paths to vehicle ground.",["Disable wire chafed through and touching body ground","Moisture in a connector creating a leak path to ground","Supervising module holding the line low permanently"],["Module A stays switched off, function unavailable","Warning message for the affected system"],3,2,["U3025","U3027","U3029","P2C97"],""],U3027:["Control Module A Disable Circuit High","U3027 is the high-side counterpart: the disable line to module A reads above its valid range, as with a short to battery voltage or a neighbouring wire. In an active-low design such as the one in Siemens patent US7596436B2, where pulling the shutdown path to ground blocks the output stages, a line stuck high means module A keeps its enable and can no longer be switched off over the hard-wired path.",["Disable wire shorted to a battery or supply wire","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in a connector","Output driver of the supervising module stuck high"],["Function locked out by the safety concept, system warning shown","Vehicle may not become ready to drive"],3,2,["U3025","U3026","U302A","P2C98"],""],U3028:["Control Module A Disable Feedback Circuit","A disable line is only useful if someone can prove it works, so many designs read back what actually arrives at the switched module. U3028 reports a fault in that feedback path for module A: the returned signal is missing or does not match the state that was commanded.",["Open feedback wire or loose pin between module A and the monitoring module","Self-test disturbed by low voltage or an early shutdown","Faulty readback stage in module A or the monitoring module"],["Function of module A blocked after the self-test, system warning","Fault may appear only at start-up or shutdown"],3,2,["U3029","U302A","U3025"],""],U3029:["Control Module A Disable Feedback Circuit Low","U3029 narrows the feedback fault to a signal that stays below its valid range, typically a readback wire shorted to ground. The consequence follows from the readback idea in GM's patent US9122662B2, where the inhibit path is driven through known test states and its actual output compared with the expected one: if the feedback is pinned low, every state that should read high fails, and the monitor cannot tell a…",["Feedback wire shorted to body ground","Moisture or corrosion pulling the readback pin low","Defective readback input stage in the monitoring module"],["Function of module A locked out, system warning displayed","Code returns at every start until the short is found"],3,2,["U3028","U302A","U3026"],""],U302A:["Control Module A Disable Feedback Circuit High","U302A means the readback from module A's disable path is stuck above its valid range, for example through a short to a supply wire. The risk is a false all-clear or a false alarm, depending on which level stands for disabled.",["Feedback wire shorted to a battery or supply wire","Corrosion bridging the readback pin to a neighbouring supply pin","Module A driving its feedback output permanently high"],["System warning and function of module A unavailable","In hybrids, possibly no ready mode or reduced drive power"],3,2,["U3028","U3029","U3027"],""],U302B:["Ignition Output Accessory/On/Start","U302B belongs to the ignition outputs, i.e. a feed that a module switches itself instead of merely reading it. The Accessory/On/Start variant should carry voltage in every power mode except Off and, unlike most accessory feeds, should stay on while the engine cranks.",["Welded relay contact keeping the feed live in Off","Faulty driver stage in the switching module, stuck on or not switching","Output wire or a connected load shorted to ground, tripping the driver protection","Blown fuse between the relay and the loads on this feed"],["Battery flat after the car has been parked","Several loads on the feed dead although the vehicle is switched on","Warning about the power supply or ignition system in the cluster"],2,0,["U300B","U302F","U302D","U302C","U3032"],""],U302C:["Ignition Output Off/On/Start","U302C covers an ignition output that encodes several states on one wire: Off, On and Start each get their own level, so a single conductor passes the power mode on to other units. It is the sending counterpart of coded inputs like the Off/Run/Crank circuit that GM's wiring manual for its 2012 light-duty trucks shows between ignition switch and body controller, which uses separate levels for key removed, key in at…",["Corroded or loose pin shifting the coded level","Faulty input in a receiving module pulling the line out of its band","Chafed wire with a partial short to ground or voltage","Faulty output stage in the sending module"],["Other modules acting on a wrong power mode, e.g. shutting down or not waking","Sporadic warnings that change with key position or button presses"],2,0,["U300C","U302B","U302D","U3031","U3011"],""],U302D:["Ignition Output On/Start","U302D concerns the output that powers the On/Start circuits, i.e. everything that has to work with the engine running and through cranking but not in Off or Accessory. On GM's 2012 pickups the body control module handles this by switching the coil of the run/crank relay over circuit 5199.",["Relay driver in the body control module staying on after shut-off","Ignition main relay contact welded or relay not pulling in","Relay coil control wire open or shorted to voltage","Retrofitted device feeding voltage back into the run/crank circuit"],["Battery repeatedly flat, often after a remote start","Engine lamp at start-up with P2535 stored in engine and transmission modules","No start or modules without power if the output fails open"],2,0,["U300D","P2535","U302E","U3030","U3023"],""],U302E:["Ignition Output On","U302E applies to an output intended to carry voltage in On alone, which means it has to switch off while the starter turns. The driving module must blank out that intended gap during cranking and judge the output only in steady power modes, otherwise every start would log the code.",["Run relay not closing, e.g. burnt contacts or open coil","Blown fuse or broken wire behind the relay","Welded contact or driver stuck on, leaving the output live in Off","Module software judging the intended cut during cranking as a fault"],["Loads on the run-only feed dead with the engine running","Power supply warning in the cluster","Battery discharged when the output stays on after shut-off"],2,0,["U300E","U302D","U302F","U3030","P2530"],""],U302F:["Ignition Output Accessory","U302F is logged by the module that switches the accessory feed for audio, sockets or windows when that feed is out of step with its own command. Two normal behaviours have to be ruled out first.",["Accessory relay welded or its driver stuck on","Accessory relay not pulling in","Blown accessory fuse or open feed wire","Retrofitted equipment overloading or backfeeding the accessory feed"],["Radio, sockets or windows dead in accessory mode","Accessories still on long after locking, battery drained"],1,0,["U300F","U3032","U302B","U302E","U3030"],"אביזרי יציאת הצתה"],U3030:["Ignition Output Start","U3030 points to the start output, the line through which a module energizes the starter relay or passes on a crank request; it should be active for seconds at most. In Tokai Rika's push-button start patents the power supply unit switches the starter relay on together with the ignition relays once brake pedal and button are confirmed, and off as soon as the engine controller reports that the engine has fired.",["Faulty start driver in the module, not switching or stuck on","Start control wire open or shorted to ground or voltage","Open or shorted coil in the starter relay loading the output","Weak battery pulling the output level down during cranking"],["Engine does not crank when start is requested","Starter keeps running or grinding after the engine has fired","Start only on a second or third attempt"],2,0,["U3010","P0615","P0616","P0617","U302D"],"התנעת יציאת הצתה"],U3031:["Ignition Output Off","U3031 relates to an output whose task is to announce the off state, for example a discrete line that tells other units they may shut down, or the off branch of a power-mode output. Shutdown in many vehicles hinges on such a signal: in Ford's patent US5945745A, modules work normally while an ignition signal is present and fall back to a sleep mode with minimal current draw once it disappears, and GM's 2012 pickups…",["Faulty output stage in the module that generates the off signal","Off-signal wire open or shorted to ground or voltage","Corroded or loose pin at the sending or receiving module","Module software setting the off output at the wrong moment"],["Battery drained because modules do not go to sleep","Functions switching off unexpectedly with the vehicle on"],2,0,["U3011","U3032","U302C","U302D","U300A"],""],U3032:["Ignition Output Accessory/Off","U3032 is the output counterpart of U3022: a line that a module drives to express the grouped state Accessory or Off, i.e. every power mode where the engine should stay off. Such grouping exists in real wiring. GM's 2012 pickup electrical manual shows a coded ignition circuit whose level is identical for a pulled key and for accessory, and changes once the key is inserted, the engine runs or cranks.",["Output stage in the driving module stuck or failed","Output wire shorted to ground or voltage, or broken","Corroded or loose pin shifting the coded level","Retrofitted accessory tapped into the line"],["Accessories such as radio or sockets not matching the key or button position","Modules staying awake after shut-off, battery drained overnight","Related ignition input codes stored in other modules"],2,0,["U3022","U302F","U3031","U302C","U302B"],""],U3033:["Control Module Security Certificate Missing/Invalid","U3033 reports that a module's own security certificate is absent or fails validation, so the unit cannot prove its identity in signed or encrypted exchanges. Stellantis uses the code in the security gateway (SGW) and in connected radios.",["Certificate not yet downloaded because the vehicle had no connectivity","Gateway software setting the code erroneously, fixed by reflash","Over-the-air update not completed","Certificate store empty or holding a wrong certificate"],["Code active or stored and cannot be cleared, usually without MIL","Security gateway not answering the diagnostic tester","Message asking for an over-the-air update or a service visit"],4,0,["U3034","U3035","U3036"],""],U3034:["Communication Authentication Key/Certificate Missing/Invalid","U3034 concerns the secret keys or certificates that modules use to authenticate messages to each other: the module finds that key material missing or not matching its partners. Ford's TRON (Trusted Real-Time Operation Network) on 2023–2025 models from F-150 to Mustang Mach-E shows the usual trigger.",["Module replaced without running the key distribution routine","Gateway software logging the code without real fault","Partner module offline during key exchange","Key storage in the module damaged"],["Code appears in several modules at once after a repair","Functions relying on secured messages unavailable or degraded","Often no noticeable symptom, sporadic entry only"],4,2,["U3033","U3035","U3036"],""],U3035:["Communication Authentication Signal Invalid Data","U3035 means a secured message arrived but its authentication part did not check out, so the receiver treats the content as invalid. In AUTOSAR Secure Onboard Communication the receiver recomputes the message authentication code over data ID, payload and freshness value; a mismatch or an unusable key counts as failed verification and the message is dropped.",["Module software rejecting valid messages, fixed by update","Keys not aligned after a module replacement","Messages checked before key initialization or wake-up finished","Corrupted frames from wiring or bus faults"],["Code found during a self-test without complaints","MIL with further network or processor codes on some engines","Function refused, e.g. gear selection not possible in the cold"],4,3,["U3036","U3034","U3033","P061B","U0140"],""],U3036:["Communication Authentication Signal Performance","U3036 judges authentication over time rather than a single bad frame: checks keep failing, cannot be completed, or sender and receiver lose step, for example in their freshness counters. AUTOSAR SecOC shows why this differs from U3035: a receiver retries when no freshness value is available or the crypto service is busy and only gives up after a configured number of build or verify attempts.",["Monitoring software flags authentication during bus sleep or wake-up","Freshness counters of sender and receiver out of step","Keys not redistributed after module replacement","Sending module intermittently missing on the bus"],["Code stored after a self-test or key-off without complaints","MIL together with P061B or U0140 on some engines","Secured functions working only intermittently"],4,1,["U3035","U3034","U3033","P061B","U0140"],""],U3500:["Control Module Input Power A Circuit Range/Performance","U3500 says that supply input A of a module is present but its voltage is implausible, for example outside the window expected for the current power mode or contradicting other measurements, without clearly passing a lower or upper limit. It thus sits between U3006, which reports a missing or open feed, and the hard limit codes U3501 and U3502. Which pin is A is up to the manufacturer;",["High-resistance terminal or fuse contact on feed A","Poor module ground shifting the measured supply","Drifting voltage measurement inside the module"],["Functions of the module dropping out or behaving inconsistently","Code returns mainly under electrical load"],2,0,["U3501","U3502","U3503","U3006","U3504"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],U3501:["Control Module Input Power A Circuit Low","U3501 reports that supply A of a module is below its permitted range. GM's electric brake booster (BSC2) in the 2016–2019 hybrid OBD tables runs two checks: the CAN/logic supply under 7.5 V for 0.09 s, and the internal sensor for the module supply under 4.9 V for 0.2 s, a level below the point where the hardware should already have shut down. Both are Special Type C, so no MIL.",["Weak or discharged 12 V battery","Deep voltage dip during engine start","Corroded fuse, terminal or ground in the A feed","Internal supply stage of the module faulty"],["Module resets or drops off the network at low voltage","Other self-tests of the module suspended","Warning lamp for the affected system, usually without MIL"],1,2,["U3502","U3500","U3503","U3006","U3505"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],U3502:["Control Module Input Power A Circuit High","U3502 means supply A rises above its allowed limit. In GM's 2016–2019 hybrid OBD tables the electric brake booster checks its CAN supply voltage and sets U3502 above 16 V lasting 0.09 s while its software runs; this is Type B, so the MIL comes on after two failing trips, and the test passes after 30 s with ignition on.",["Generator regulator or DC/DC converter overcharging","Jump start or external charger with excessive voltage","Loose battery terminal causing voltage spikes","Faulty voltage measurement inside the module"],["MIL after repeated trips","Several modules logging overvoltage at once","Flickering lights or battery warning"],2,3,["U3501","U3500","U3503","U3506","U350A"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],U3503:["Control Module Input Power A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","U3503 stands for a supply A that keeps jumping: mostly correct, but with brief dropouts or spikes, so the module sees erratic readings or restarts. What sets it apart from U3501 and U3502 is the pattern rather than the level: short interruptions, fast swings between samples or repeated resets. No manufacturer documents U3503 publicly.",["Loose crimp, pin or fuse contact in feed A","Chafed wire making intermittent contact","Ground shared with heavy loads causing dips","Cracked solder joint inside the module"],["Sporadic resets or brief function dropouts","Code returns over bumps or when loads switch"],2,0,["U3500","U3501","U3502","U3507","U350B"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],U3504:["Control Module Input Power B Circuit Range/Performance","U3504 checks the plausibility of the second supply input, B. Modules with high-power stages often split their supply: in GM's electric brake booster tables B is the battery feed of the booster circuit (voltage sensor 1), checked separately against low and high limits and compared with feed C.",["Resistance in fuse, connector or ground of feed B under load","Feed B supplied from a different source than expected","Drifting measurement of feed B inside the module"],["Power stage functions weak or switched off under load","Code mainly when motors or valves are active"],2,2,["U3505","U3506","U3507","U3007","U3018"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],U3505:["Control Module Input Power B Circuit Low","U3505 reports that supply input B is too low. In GM's 2016–2019 hybrid tables the electric brake booster treats B as the battery feed of the booster circuit and checks it at several levels: sensor reading under 6 V for 30 s, battery voltage under 9.3 V for 90 s, and quick 0.2 s checks with reduced assist once it falls below 9.3 V (level 1) or 7.5 V (level 2); all Special Type C, no MIL.",["Fuse of feed B blown by a short elsewhere on the circuit","Weak or discharged 12 V battery","Corroded terminal or ground in feed B","Internal measurement or supply path faulty"],["Functions on the second feed missing, e.g. warm A/C","Reduced brake assist with warning on booster modules","Stored together with U3018"],1,2,["U3506","U3504","U3507","U3018","U3007"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],U3506:["Control Module Input Power B Circuit High","U3506 reports overvoltage on supply input B. In GM's electric brake booster (2016–2019 hybrid OBD tables) three checks feed this code: battery voltage of the booster circuit above 17 V for 90 s, the supply of the internal motor driver above 18 V for 1.1 s, and battery voltage above 16.5 V for 1.1 s, at which booster performance is cut back. All are Type B, MIL after two trips; passing takes 90 s with ignition on.",["Charging voltage too high from regulator or DC/DC converter","Jump starter or charger delivering excessive voltage","Loose battery terminal causing spikes","Faulty measurement of feed B in the module"],["MIL after two trips","Reduced assist of the supplied power stage","Overvoltage codes in further modules"],2,3,["U3505","U3504","U3507","U3502","U350A"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],U3507:["Control Module Input Power B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","U3507 covers an unsteady supply B: the voltage is mostly in range but drops out or jumps for short moments. Since B often powers stages such as motors or valves, the dropouts typically appear when these draw current, for instance while braking or steering. GM's brake booster tables show that the module judges B over short and long windows (0.2 s up to 90 s);",["Loose crimp or worn fuse holder in feed B","Corroded ground point of the module","Chafed wire with intermittent contact"],["Brief function dropouts when power stages switch on","Code returns sporadically and is hard to reproduce"],2,2,["U3504","U3505","U3506","U3503","U3018"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],U3508:["Control Module Input Power C Circuit Range/Performance","U3508 checks the plausibility of a third supply input, C. Only modules with large or separately protected loads have three feeds; in GM's electric brake booster (2016–2019 hybrid tables) C is the motor driver feed, measured by voltage sensor 2 and compared with feed B through U3019 (ratio outside 0.766 to 1.321).",["Resistance in the motor supply path of feed C","Poor ground of the power stage","Drift of the internal voltage divider"],["Reduced function of the motor-driven system","Correlation codes between feeds stored as well"],2,2,["U3509","U350A","U350B","U3019","U3013"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],U3509:["Control Module Input Power C Circuit Low","U3509 says supply C is too low. In GM's 2016–2019 hybrid OBD tables the electric brake booster sets it when voltage sensor 2, which watches the motor driver supply, reads below 6 V for 90 s while the car travels faster than 4 mph.",["Fuse of the motor supply open","Broken wire or failed connector in feed C","Deeply discharged 12 V battery","Internal measurement of feed C faulty"],["MIL and brake warning on the first trip","Harder brake pedal through missing assist"],2,3,["U350A","U3508","U350B","U3019","U3013"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],U350A:["Control Module Input Power C Circuit High","U350A is the overvoltage code for supply C. GM's electric brake booster (2016–2019 hybrid tables) logs it when voltage sensor 2 on the motor driver supply exceeds 19.8 V for 90 s at speeds above 4 mph, Type A, so a single failing trip lights the MIL.",["Generator regulator or DC/DC converter overcharging","Jump start from a 24 V source","Faulty measurement of feed C inside the module"],["MIL and brake warning on the first trip","Brake assist reduced or switched off"],2,3,["U3509","U3508","U350B","U3506","U3502"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],U350B:["Control Module Input Power C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","U350B reports that supply C fluctuates: it drops or spikes briefly without staying out of range. Where C feeds a motor stage, as in GM's electric brake booster (motor driver supply, voltage sensor 2), such faults surface at moments of peak current, because a loose contact then loses voltage or opens for an instant.",["Loose fuse contact or ring terminal in feed C or its ground","Chafed wire near the module","Corroded connector pins"],["Brief loss of assist from the motor-driven function","Sporadic warning lamp that clears again"],2,2,["U3508","U3509","U350A","U3507","U3019"],"כוח כניסת מודול בקרה‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],U350C:["Control Module Cooling Fan Circuit/Open","U350C reports that the fan built into or attached to a control module draws no current, or its circuit is open, at the moment the module switches it on. Some electronics carry their own blower: on the 2021 Toyota RAV4 Prime the plug-in charger has a fan with a speed sensor (bulletin T-SB-0021-21, code P1CE931), and the central infotainment unit of the Karma Revero has one under a shroud (TB-24-94-01).",["Fan motor winding or brushes open","Fan plug loose or not latched after the module was removed","Broken fan supply or control wire","Fan output stage inside the module failed open"],["Module fan silent when it should run","Module overheats, reduces output, charges slower or restarts","Temperature warning or function message for the affected module"],2,2,["U350D","U350E","U350F","P0480"],"מאוורר קירור מודול בקרה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],U350D:["Control Module Cooling Fan Circuit Low","U350D is set when the voltage or current feedback in a control module's fan circuit sits below the window the module expects. Usually the fan supply or control wire touches ground, or the motor itself has shorted turns, so the output stage limits current or switches off and the fan stands still; a blown fan fuse produces the same picture.",["Fan supply or control wire chafed through to ground","Fan motor with shorted windings drawing excess current","Fan fuse blown as a result of the short","Output stage in the module pulling the line low"],["Module fan does not run","Reduced function or shutdown of the module when hot","Blown fan fuse"],2,2,["U350C","U350E","U350F","P0691"],"מאוורר קירור מודול בקרה — אות נמוך במעגל"],U350E:["Control Module Cooling Fan Circuit High","U350E points to a fan circuit whose level is higher than the module expects, typically because the control or feedback line is shorted to battery voltage or the output stage is stuck on. Unlike the low and open faults, the fan may then run all the time, even with the module cold or the car parked, which is audible and can drain the 12 V battery.",["Fan control or feedback wire shorted to a 12 V supply","Fan output stage in the module stuck on","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the fan connector"],["Module fan running continuously, also after switch-off","12 V battery discharged after standing","Fan does not react to temperature changes"],2,0,["U350C","U350D","U350F","P0692"],"מאוורר קירור מודול בקרה — אות גבוה במעגל"],U350F:["Control Module Cooling Fan Circuit Range/Performance","U350F means the fan circuit is electrically sound but the fan does not do what it is told: its speed feedback disagrees with the command, or the module keeps heating up although the fan is switched on. Dust, a blocked or rubbing blade, worn bearings or a lost speed signal are typical.",["Fan blade blocked by dust, debris or a deformed shroud","Worn fan bearing slowing the fan down","Fan speed sensor signal missing or misread","Module software misjudging the fan feedback (Toyota RAV4 Prime charger)"],["Fan noise, rattling or whining from the module","Module runs hot, charging or function slowed","Code returns after clearing once the fan is commanded again"],2,2,["U350C","U350D","U350E","P0480"],"מאוורר קירור מודול בקרה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],U3510:["Control Module Missing Calibration","U3510 says a control module lacks a calibration it needs: either the data set that adapts its software to the vehicle was never written or got lost, or a learned calibration such as a sensor alignment has not been done. CARB makes every emission-critical unit report a calibration ID and a verification number, so empty or invalid data cannot pass unnoticed.",["New or used module installed without programming or setup","Software update aborted, e.g. by low 12 V voltage or lost connection","Required learn or alignment routine not performed after repair","Internal memory of the module losing its stored data"],["Function of the affected module unavailable or limited","Warning lamp of the related system, MIL if the module is OBD-relevant","Fault appears right after a module replacement or software update"],4,3,["P0602","P0630","P0601","P062F"],"מודול בקרה — חסר כיול"],U3511:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit B","U3511 is the general fault of a second high-voltage interlock loop, circuit B. Many vehicles need more than one loop: a Volvo truck patent gives each separate HV bus its own interlock circuit, and a Samsung SDI patent describes extra loops for battery-internal parts such as the service disconnect or the junction box, each with its own source, detector and diagnosis.",["HV connector, cover or disconnect in loop B open or not latched after service","Bent, pushed-back or corroded interlock pins","Interlock wiring of loop B chafed or cut","Source or sense stage for loop B in the monitoring module faulty"],["Vehicle does not enter ready mode","High-voltage or hybrid system warning in the cluster","Charging refused"],3,3,["U3512","U3513","U3514","U3515","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ B"],U3512:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit B Performance","U3512 is stored when interlock loop B still conducts but behaves implausibly: its resistance drifts outside the permitted window, the returned signal does not follow the test pattern in time, or two readings of the same loop disagree. CATL's interlock patent explains why loops misreport: contact impedance between HV parts, supply fluctuations and static discharge can cause false alarms.",["Oxidised interlock pins raising the loop resistance","Connector in loop B seated but not fully latched","Harness rubbing on the body with intermittent contact","Interference or supply ripple distorting the loop signal"],["HV system switches off and on again unexpectedly","Ready mode lost while driving or at start","Interlock codes in several modules at once"],3,3,["U3511","U3513","U3514","U3516","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3513:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit B Low","U3513 reports a signal on interlock loop B that stays below its lower limit while the loop is energised by the module. What that means depends on the circuit: where the module feeds a test voltage in and reads it back at the far end, an opened plug reads low just like a wire touching ground.",["Interlock wire of loop B chafed through to ground","Plug or cover in loop B open, read as low by the sensing circuit","Pushed-back interlock terminal without contact","Interlock source in the monitoring module not delivering its signal"],["No ready mode, HV contactors stay open","Hybrid or EV warning lamp, MIL depending on maker","Charging not possible"],3,3,["U3511","U3512","U3514","U3517","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ B — ערך נמוך"],U3514:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit B High","U3514 means loop B reads higher than allowed: a wire of the loop touches 12 V or another supply, or the loop does not fall back to its low state once the module turns its source off. GM's loop A code checks both states, allowing 24 % of 5 V while the source is off and 44 % while it is on.",["Interlock wire of loop B shorted to 12 V or another supply","Interlock source in the module not switching off","Water in a connector bridging an interlock pin to a supply pin","Incorrect splice or add-on wiring after a repair"],["Vehicle will not start or enter ready mode","Service or HV warning lamp on","Fault stays present with all HV connectors properly mated"],3,3,["U3511","U3512","U3513","U3518","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ B — ערך גבוה"],U3515:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit C","U3515 is the general fault of a third interlock loop, circuit C. Such a loop exists where one or two are not enough: Caterpillar's patent for battery machines forms a separate interlock circuit from each battery group with its disconnect and contactor pair, and Samsung SDI mentions designs with more than two independent loops for parts inside the pack.",["Connector or cover belonging to loop C opened during work and not refitted correctly","Interlock harness of loop C damaged","Fault in a coupled loop opening loop C as well","Monitoring module unable to drive or read loop C"],["No ready mode, HV system switched off","Interlock codes for more than one loop stored together","Charging blocked"],3,3,["U3516","U3517","U3518","U3511","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ C"],U3516:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit C Performance","U3516 flags loop C as electrically present but untrustworthy: resistance, timing or pattern of the returned signal fall outside what the module accepts, often only for moments. As the U35xx series has no intermittent code for loops B and C, unlike P0A0E for loop A, short dropouts will probably be stored here.",["Loose or spread contact in a connector of loop C","Oxidised low-voltage interlock pins","Twisted or strained harness section moving with the body","Static discharge or interference on the interlock line"],["Sporadic loss of ready mode","HV warning that appears and clears by itself","Fault hard to reproduce in the workshop"],3,3,["U3515","U3517","U3518","U3512","P0A0E"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3517:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit C Low","U3517 says the level read back on interlock loop C stays too low. Depending on the design, an opened plug in loop C, a wire chafed to ground or a failed source in the monitoring module all lead to it. In current-fed designs such as the Texas Instruments reference circuit, a short to ground draws extra supply current while an opened loop does not, which helps to separate the two.",["Interlock wire of loop C chafed to ground at a module or the body","Connector in loop C unplugged, sensed as a low signal","Broken interlock connector housing or terminal","Source stage for loop C failed in the monitoring module"],["Vehicle cannot be started","HV system warning in the instrument cluster","Charging unavailable"],3,3,["U3515","U3516","U3518","U3513","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ C — ערך נמוך"],U3518:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit C High","U3518 is stored when loop C reads above its upper limit, usually a loop wire shorted to 12 V, to the wire of another loop in a shared connector, or a source stage that no longer switches off. Volvo's two-loop patent couples loops only through a galvanically isolated relay, so foreign voltage from one loop is not meant to reach another; where wires of different loops share a connector, damage can still bridge them.",["Interlock wire of loop C shorted to 12 V","Loop C bridged to another loop's wire in a shared connector","Interlock source for loop C stuck on in the module"],["No ready mode despite all HV connectors being in place","Service or HV warning lamp lit","High codes for more than one interlock loop"],3,3,["U3515","U3516","U3517","U3514","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ C — ערך גבוה"],U3519:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit D","U3519 marks a fault on the fourth interlock loop of the high-voltage system, circuit D, that the module does not classify further. A fourth independent loop mainly makes sense where one vehicle carries several battery packs.",["Disconnect of the battery group on loop D left open or not locked after charging or service","Connector in loop D not fully latched","Loop D wiring damaged between packs or distribution units","Controller that drives and reads loop D faulty"],["One battery pack or high-voltage branch not available","Reduced range or power, or no ready mode at all, depending on design","High-voltage system warning in the instrument cluster"],3,3,["U351A","U351B","U351C","U351D","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ D"],U351A:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit D Performance","U351A says that loop D returns a signal, but not the one the module sent out. Many designs feed the loop with pulses rather than a steady level. In a Corun battery patent a microcontroller sends a 0 to 5 V square wave at 100 Hz with half on, half off through the interlock switches of pack, motor controller and vehicle controller, and treats the loop as sound only if frequency, on-time and amplitude return unchanged.",["Corroded or worn interlock contacts adding resistance to loop D","Moisture in a low-voltage connector of the loop","Loop wiring routed too close to switching high-voltage cables","Signal input of the evaluating controller faulty"],["Sudden loss of high-voltage power while driving or charging","Fault appears after rain, washing or on rough roads","Restart sometimes possible after switching off and on"],3,3,["U3519","U351B","U351C","U351E","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U351B:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit D Low","U351B reports that too little level comes back from interlock loop D while the module drives it. GM's hybrid tables for the loop A code P0A0C give a frame of reference: the test only runs when on-board voltage exceeds 10.2 V, judges what fraction of a 5 V test signal returns against a 30 % limit and logs a Type A fault after two failed 12.5 ms readings.",["Loop D wire pinched against the body and shorted to ground","Plug within loop D not seated after a repair","Test voltage source in the controller failed"],["No ready mode or high-voltage branch D unavailable","Warning to have the high-voltage system checked","Fault stays present after clearing until the wiring is repaired"],3,3,["U3519","U351A","U351C","U351F","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ D — ערך נמוך"],U351C:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit D High","U351C is stored when loop D carries more voltage than its present state allows. GM's high check for loop A, P0A0D, shows why both states are tested: with the source commanded to 0 V, more than 24 % of 5 V counts as a failure, five times in eight samples; with the source at 5 V the limit is 44 %, four times in six.",["Loop D wire in contact with a 12 V supply line","Source driver in the controller no longer switches off","Earlier repair splice joined the loop to a wrong wire"],["Vehicle does not reach ready mode","Fault returns immediately after clearing","Other 12 V consumers may show faults if a supply wire is involved"],3,3,["U3519","U351A","U351B","U3520","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ D — ערך גבוה"],U351D:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit E","U351D covers a disturbed fifth interlock loop, circuit E, where the module cannot narrow the fault down. Five loops arise naturally if every protected housing gets its own circuit. A GM patent describes this: each high-voltage enclosure has a functional interlock tied to its access point, and the low-voltage signal inside only gets through while that opening is closed.",["Cover of a high-voltage housing on loop E not fitted or not fully tightened","Interlock contact or bridge in the cover bent or broken","Loop E wiring damaged between housings","Evaluating controller faulty"],["No ready mode after work on a high-voltage component","High-voltage warning in the instrument cluster"],3,3,["U351E","U351F","U3520","U3519","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ E"],U351E:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit E Performance","U351E points to loop E giving results the module cannot trust, and the doubt may concern the monitoring hardware as much as the wiring. Designers do test their own test circuits: CATL first checks its current-generating stage so that a failing source is not blamed on high-voltage parts, and Sanden's interlock at the plug of an electric A/C compressor also recognises defects of the monitoring device and its loop, not…",["Current or voltage source for loop E drifting in the controller","Loose contact in a loop E connector","Detection circuit or its reference faulty","Controller software with outdated plausibility limits"],["High-voltage shutdowns without a recognisable pattern","Fault returns although wiring and connectors test good","Possibly further self-test codes in the same controller"],4,3,["U351D","U351F","U3520","U351A","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ E — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U351F:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit E Low","U351F reports a low reading on interlock loop E, the usual result when a plug in that loop is separated or one of its wires is grounded. The US standard FMVSS 305a explains the hurry: a high-voltage connector that can be pulled without tools may, as one permitted option, bring its live parts to 60 V DC or less within one second of separation. The interlock gives the early signal for that;",["High-voltage plug with interlock in loop E pulled or backed out","Loop E wire chafed through to ground","Interlock pin pushed back in its housing"],["Abrupt loss of drive power, often with a stop-safely message","Vehicle cannot be restarted in ready mode","Charging aborted or impossible"],3,3,["U351D","U351E","U3520","U351B","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ E — ערך נמוך"],U3520:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit E High","U3520 means the fifth interlock loop sits above its permitted range, usually because a loop wire has picked up battery voltage or another low-voltage feed. Lear's patent for a pulsed interlock tester shows how to pin this down further: it measures current at generator and detector pins and, by comparing them, works out at which end the unwanted link to the 12 V side lies.",["Loop E wire shorted to a 12 V supply","Water or corrosion bridging a loop pin to a supply pin","Loop source in the controller stuck on"],["No ready mode, high-voltage warning shown","Fault reappears directly after clearing"],3,3,["U351D","U351E","U351F","U351C","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ E — ערך גבוה"],U3521:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit F","U3521 flags an unspecified fault in loop F, the sixth interlock loop. Extra loops often guard service openings rather than cables. FMVSS 305a defines the service disconnect as the device that switches the circuit off for checks and service and demands finger protection wherever it opens without tools; its interlock tells the controller when it is pulled.",["Service disconnect not fully inserted or its lever not locked","Cover with interlock magnet missing, swapped or mounted out of position","Reed relay or switch contact of the cover interlock failed","Loop F wiring damaged"],["No ready mode after battery or service work","High-voltage system message in the cluster"],3,3,["U3522","U3523","U3524","U351D","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ F"],U3522:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit F Performance","U3522 is set when loop F behaves inconsistently, for instance when redundant evaluation channels reach different verdicts or the signal timing is off. Such checks exist because the interlock belongs to a safety function: Samsung SDI notes that it then needs an ASIL rating and failure-rate figures for its parts, so hidden faults in the monitoring path have to be caught, not just an open loop.",["Redundant measuring channels for loop F disagree because of a sensing fault","Intermittent contact in a loop F connector","Internal fault of the evaluating controller"],["Ready mode occasionally refused, then available again","High-voltage warning that comes and goes"],4,3,["U3521","U3523","U3524","U351E","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ F — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3523:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit F Low","U3523 is logged when loop F reads too low, typically from an open plug or a wire shorted to ground. Tracing it means working close to high-voltage parts. The German statutory accident insurance DGUV lets only trained high-voltage staff de-energise the system and insists on the order: isolate, secure against switching back on, then prove absence of voltage with a suitable tester, not a multimeter.",["Plug in loop F open or not engaged after service","Loop F wire shorted to ground","Broken interlock connector housing or locking tab"],["Vehicle not ready to drive, high-voltage warning shown","Charging not possible"],4,3,["U3521","U3522","U3524","U351F","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ F — ערך נמוך"],U3524:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit F High","U3524 indicates a level on loop F above its upper threshold. Pulsed test schemes recognise this easily: if the loop is driven with a fixed square wave, as in Corun's 100 Hz battery design, a wire stuck at 12 V returns a flat level without any edges, which no intact connection could produce.",["Loop F wire chafed against a fused 12 V wire","Loop pin bridged to a neighbouring supply pin by corrosion or a bent terminal","Source driver for loop F no longer switches off"],["High-voltage system remains off, vehicle not ready","Code returns at once after clearing"],3,3,["U3521","U3522","U3523","U3520","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ F — ערך גבוה"],U3525:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit G","U3525 stands for a fault on the seventh interlock loop, circuit G, that the module does not classify further. Auxiliary high-voltage consumers are candidates for loops of their own: Sanden runs an interlock loop beside the HV plug between an electric A/C compressor and the traction battery, and a Chinese design cited by Caterpillar links an air-conditioning interlock circuit to the main one over CAN.",["HV plug of an auxiliary consumer such as compressor or heater not latched","Loop G wiring to the auxiliary consumer damaged","Interlock contacts inside the consumer's connector damaged","Evaluating controller faulty"],["Air conditioning or electric heater unavailable","In some designs no ready mode at all","High-voltage or climate warning in the cluster"],3,3,["U3526","U3527","U3528","U3521","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ G"],U3526:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit G Performance","U3526 reports an implausible result for loop G. Not every interlock is a wire loop: Rivian patented a virtual interlock in which a controller first brings the DC bus up to a low, safe voltage only, gathers the voltages that the high-voltage components report over CAN, and raises the bus to operating voltage only if those reports are acceptable.",["Voltage sensing inside one high-voltage component faulty","Voltage message missing or late on the CAN bus","HV plug not fully seated, so one component sees no bus voltage"],["Start-up of the high-voltage system aborted","Communication codes in other control units at the same time"],4,3,["U3525","U3527","U3528","U3522","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ G — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3527:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit G Low","U3527 sets when the level on loop G drops below what the module expects. When several controllers watch interlock lines, the reporting unit already narrows the search. A Mercedes service bulletin on the 243 model series shows this with loop A codes: the DC charging unit and the AC charger each store a ground-short code, the battery management a short to positive, and the PTC heater has a separate code.",["Loop G wire cut or chafed to ground near a control unit","Plug in the section of the reporting unit not connected","Loop source of the reporting controller failed"],["Vehicle does not become ready, or charging is refused","Interlock codes in more than one control unit"],3,3,["U3525","U3526","U3528","U3523","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ G — ערך נמוך"],U3528:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit G High","U3528 means something lifts loop G to a level the controller never expects from it. Texas Instruments notes that automotive interlocks, unlike industrial ones, must survive a short to the 12 V battery and to ground; its reference design feeds the loop through an intelligent switch on the supply side with current limiting and thermal shutdown.",["Loop G wire shorted to the 12 V supply","Loop output stage damaged by an earlier short and stuck on","Moisture bridging pins in a loop G connector"],["No ready mode, high-voltage warning","Code persists after the harness repair"],3,3,["U3525","U3526","U3527","U3524","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ G — ערך גבוה"],U3529:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit H","U3529 marks a fault on circuit H, the eighth interlock loop, without a more specific result. Texas Instruments distinguishes one central loop running through all high-voltage parts from individual loops inside each subsystem that confirm its own assembly.",["Connector or disconnect on loop H open","Loop H wiring damaged on chassis or between packs","Code logged by a controller with faulty software rather than a real loop H fault"],["One HV branch or pack unavailable, or no ready mode","Warning about the high-voltage system"],3,3,["U352A","U352B","U352C","U3525","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ H"],U352A:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit H Performance","U352A says the eighth loop is closed but its electrical values leave the calibrated band. In CATL's interlock patent the decision thresholds follow from the loop current, a sensing resistor and the impedance of every HV part in the chain. A long loop through many parts therefore has narrow margins: each extra contact, a replacement part with different internal resistance or a lengthened harness shifts the result.",["Replacement HV component with different interlock resistance fitted","Extra connector or harness extension added to loop H","Rising contact resistance at several loop H terminals"],["Fault appears after a repair or conversion","High-voltage system switches off occasionally"],4,3,["U3529","U352B","U352C","U3526","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ H — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U352B:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit H Low","U352B reports too low a level on interlock loop H. Apart from a pulled plug or a grounded wire, a deliberate opening can cause it: Texas Instruments mentions feeding a crash signal into the loop so that high voltage shuts off after an accident. The DGUV warns that such a crash shutdown does not establish absence of voltage and that disconnection following the maker's rescue sheet is still advisable;",["Loop H opened on purpose by a crash signal after an accident","Loop H wiring or plug damaged in a collision","Loop H wire shorted to ground"],["High voltage off after an accident or airbag deployment","Vehicle cannot be made ready"],4,3,["U3529","U352A","U352C","U3527","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ H — ערך נמוך"],U352C:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit H High","U352C reports an excessive reading on loop H. Whether that points to foreign voltage or to a break depends on the quantity the controller evaluates. If it reads voltage, a wire touching 12 V is the usual reason. If it works out the loop's resistance, as Lear's tester patent does, a value beyond the maximum is treated as open and one under the minimum as shorted, so high may mean corrosion or a loose terminal.",["Loop H wire in contact with a 12 V supply","Corroded or loose terminal raising loop H resistance","Loop source stuck on in the controller"],["No ready mode, high-voltage warning","Fault sometimes disappears after moving connectors"],3,3,["U3529","U352A","U352B","U3528","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ H — ערך גבוה"],U352D:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit J","U352D is the summary code for interlock circuit J, the ninth loop in J2012 lettering, which leaves out the letter I. What the loop contains is up to the maker, and none has published it. A loop need not pass through plugs only: a Ford patent for a centralised interlock leads the circuit across mating body parts such as the hood or trunk latch and its receptacle, so that opening the lid by itself switches high…",["Connector in loop J not fully latched","Hood, trunk or access panel latch wired into loop J not fully engaged","Loop J wiring damaged","Controller that drives and reads loop J faulty"],["No ready mode, often right after a hood, trunk or underbody panel was opened","High-voltage system warning in the instrument cluster","Charging blocked"],3,3,["U352E","U352F","U3530","U3529","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ J"],U352E:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit J Performance","U352E reports an implausible result from loop J. Interlocks also guard auxiliary drives outside the traction system. Copeland patented a contactless version for the inverter of a trailer refrigeration unit, which may be fed from a 460 V generator through a rectifier at about 650 V DC: a magnet on each terminal cover faces a Hall sensor in the housing, and the drive releases voltage only while that field is sensed.",["Cover with interlock sensing seated unevenly or gasket deformed","Loose contact in a loop J connector","Sensing element or its actuating magnet loose or damaged","Signal input of the evaluating controller faulty"],["High-voltage consumer on loop J switching off intermittently","Fault more frequent on rough roads or after work on covers","High-voltage system warning that comes and goes"],3,3,["U352D","U352F","U3530","U352A","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ J — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U352F:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit J Low","U352F means loop J reads below its lower threshold, the picture an interrupted loop gives. In high-voltage plugs the interlock pins are shorter than the power pins, so they part first when the plug is withdrawn.",["High-voltage plug in loop J partly withdrawn, interlock pins already apart","Interlock pin in loop J pushed back in its cavity","Loop J wire chafed through to ground"],["High-voltage system switches off and stays off","No ready mode after work near high-voltage plugs","Charging not possible"],3,3,["U352D","U352E","U3530","U352B","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ J — ערך נמוך"],U3530:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit J High","U3530 flags loop J above its upper threshold. Foreign voltage is one explanation, but in a design that pushes a constant current through the loop and reads the drop across it, any added resistance lifts the measured value too. Tesla's HVIL tech note for early Model S cars, filed with NHTSA, names a poor solder joint at a charger board connector that exceeded 90 ohms only when hot.",["Cracked solder joint or crimp in loop J whose resistance rises when warm","Loop J wire in contact with a 12 V supply","Loose or spread terminal in a loop J connector"],["Fault appears after long drives or charging, not on a cold start","Charging session or drive interrupted by a high-voltage warning","Loop measures normal once the components have cooled down"],4,3,["U352D","U352E","U352F","U352C","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ J — ערך גבוה"],U3531:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit K","U3531 stands for an unspecified fault on interlock circuit K, the tenth loop. An interlock need not be a dedicated wire pair. For hybrid trucks, International patented running the hybrid CAN bus through the same connector as the power cable: once the plug is parted, data traffic on that bus stops and one terminating impedance drops out, and a traffic detector then opens an interrupter in the high-voltage feed.",["Connector in loop K not fully latched","Communication line routed with loop K interrupted or disturbed","Loop K wiring damaged","Controller monitoring loop K faulty"],["No ready mode or one high-voltage branch unavailable","Network or communication codes stored alongside","High-voltage system warning in the instrument cluster"],3,3,["U3532","U3533","U3534","U352D","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ K"],U3532:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit K Performance","U3532 indicates that loop K does not respond the way the controller expects. Some checks run only while the system powers up. A Ford patent describes one: during precharge a switch holds the high-voltage bus between an upper and a lower level far below operating voltage, and the interlock test takes place inside that window.",["Marginal contact in a loop K connector that passes some start checks and fails others","Fault in the precharge path disturbing the start-up check","Controller software with outdated check limits"],["Vehicle sometimes does not become ready at switch-on, then works on the next attempt","Fault stored at start-up rather than while driving"],3,3,["U3531","U3533","U3534","U352E","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ K — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3533:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit K Low","U3533 says loop K reads too low. Apart from an open plug, part of the loop current may be escaping somewhere. Tesla's HVIL tech note for the Model S describes two such cases: a drive inverter whose control board leaked some of the nominal 20 mA loop current to ground, and a loop wire squeezed against ground close to a seat belt pretensioner. The fault therefore need not sit in a connector at all;",["Loop K wire squeezed against ground by seat, trim or mounting parts","Plug within loop K not connected","High-voltage component on loop K leaking loop current to ground internally"],["Vehicle does not reach ready mode","Fault may follow work on seats or interior trim","Warning to have the high-voltage system checked"],3,3,["U3531","U3532","U3534","U352F","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ K — ערך נמוך"],U3534:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit K High","U3534 reports loop K above its upper threshold. Besides a loop wire chafed onto a 12 V feed, the timing of the electronics can be behind it. In the Texas Instruments reference design TIDA-020069 a 10 mA constant current feeds the loop, and that source can be disabled to save power or to hold the loop in a deliberate fault state until the other systems are ready.",["Loop K wire in contact with a 12 V supply","Loop source still disabled when the controller evaluates loop K","Controller software with faulty start-up sequence"],["Vehicle does not become ready","Fault may appear right at switch-on although no wiring damage is found"],4,3,["U3531","U3532","U3533","U3530","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ K — ערך גבוה"],U3535:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit L","U3535 is the umbrella code for interlock circuit L, the eleventh loop. Large vehicles carry many guarded compartments. On New Flyer battery buses the energy storage units sit on the roof at front, centre and rear, and each access door is watched by an interlock limit switch.",["Door or lid limit switch on loop L misadjusted or not actuated","Manual high-voltage interlock or lockout switch left off after service","Connector in loop L not fully latched","Controller monitoring loop L faulty"],["Vehicle or one energy storage unit unavailable after maintenance","High-voltage system warning on the dashboard","Fault linked to opening or closing a compartment"],3,3,["U3536","U3537","U3538","U3531","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ L"],U3536:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit L Performance","U3536 means loop L delivers values the controller considers implausible without a clear limit being crossed. Shaky contacts are a typical reason. Tesla's Model S HVIL note has technicians wiggle each plug while a second person watches the live loop voltage, and stresses that a weak spot may make the value drift long before it is bad enough to set a fault; pin drag tests then reveal loose terminal tension.",["Terminal in a loop L connector with too little contact force","Loop L connector without proper strain relief, moving with vibration","Signal input of the evaluating controller faulty"],["Short high-voltage dropouts while driving, especially over bumps","Warning disappears after a restart"],3,3,["U3535","U3537","U3538","U3532","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ L — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3537:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit L Low","U3537 is logged for an insufficient reading on loop L. The cause may lie outside the loop itself. In a Volvo patent with paired loops for trucks with separate high-voltage buses, neither loop is closed before the current sources start; one loop only closes once the source of the other energises the coil of an isolated relay.",["Plug within loop L disconnected or wire shorted to ground","Source of a coupled loop not running, so the coupling relay stays open","Coupling relay between loops with failed coil or contact"],["Vehicle or one high-voltage bus does not become ready","Interlock codes for more than one loop stored at once"],3,3,["U3535","U3536","U3538","U3533","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ L — ערך נמוך"],U3538:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit L High","U3538 is stored when loop L overshoots its permitted maximum. In a constant-current loop that can be a contact problem rather than foreign voltage. Tesla's Model S tech note records its most frequent HVIL field failure as high-voltage plugs serving the cabin PTC heater, the heater for battery coolant and the A/C compressor harness whose interlock pins were too short: the supplier had changed the housing without…",["Connector revision in loop L with interlock pins too short for reliable contact","Loop L wire in contact with a 12 V supply","Spread female terminal in a loop L connector"],["Vehicle does not become ready or switches off high voltage","Heating or air conditioning affected if their plugs are part of the loop"],3,3,["U3535","U3536","U3537","U3534","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ L — ערך גבוה"],U3539:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit M","U3539 covers a non-specific fault on circuit M, the twelfth interlock loop. Loops J to M only make sense in very extensive high-voltage systems such as trucks, buses, construction or mining machines with interfaces for battery, charging, drive and auxiliaries such as hydraulic pumps or heaters.",["Connector of an auxiliary or charging interface in loop M not fully latched","Loop M wiring damaged on a long run through the vehicle","Controller monitoring loop M faulty"],["Vehicle or a high-voltage auxiliary unavailable","High-voltage warning without visible damage"],3,3,["U353A","U353B","U353C","U3535","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ M"],U353A:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit M Performance","U353A flags loop M as questionable rather than plainly open or shorted. Redundant monitoring can produce exactly that state. NIO patented an interlock fed by two signal generators whose pulse trains overlap on one line; with duty ratios A and B the detector expects a combined average of A plus B minus their product.",["One of the loop M signal sources weak or failed","Loose contact in a loop M connector distorting the signal","Detection circuit for loop M faulty"],["Warning lamp while the vehicle keeps driving","Occasional loss of high voltage if the second channel also degrades"],4,3,["U3539","U353B","U353C","U3536","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ M — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U353B:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit M Low","U353B is set when loop M reads too low. A lever-type plug can leave it in exactly that state on purpose. A connector patent by Hyundai and Kia adds an intermediate lock to the lever: on the way out it stops at a point where the interlock contacts are already apart while the power terminals still touch, so the system has time to switch off before the second lever movement separates the plug.",["Lever-type connector in loop M left at its intermediate position","Loop M wire shorted to ground","Loop M source in the controller failed"],["No ready mode after service on high-voltage plugs","Fault persists after clearing"],3,3,["U3539","U353A","U353C","U3537","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ M — ערך נמוך"],U353C:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit M High","U353C indicates that loop M exceeds its upper threshold. A loop built from known resistances can be checked point by point. In Tesla's Model S tech note the battery management sends a constant 20 mA through four resistance stages of 60 ohms, 240 ohms in total, so about 4.8 V appears at the start and the value falls to 3.6, 2.4 and 1.2 V at the following connectors.",["Corroded or loose contact adding resistance in one section of loop M","Loop M wire in contact with a 12 V supply","High-voltage component with internal loop resistance out of specification"],["Vehicle does not become ready","High-voltage warning returns after clearing"],3,3,["U3539","U353A","U353B","U3538","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ M — ערך גבוה"],U353D:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit N","U353D is the general code for interlock circuit N, the thirteenth loop in J2012 lettering; designs with that many loops are only conceivable on very large high-voltage systems. No maker documents U353D publicly.",["Water in a loop N connector because a seal is pinched or damaged","Connector in loop N not fully seated","Interlock pins corroded after earlier moisture","Controller that drives and reads loop N faulty"],["No ready mode or no start, often after rain, washing or wading","Isolation fault stored alongside the interlock code","Hybrid or high-voltage system warning in the cluster"],3,3,["U353E","U353F","U3540","U3539","P0A0A","P0AA6"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ N"],U353E:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit N Performance","U353E marks loop N as implausible. Such a verdict can stem from electrical interference rather than from the loop wiring. Tesla bulletin SB-25-17-005 for 2023 and 2024 Model Y cars describes the centre high mounted stop lamp disturbing the supply line of the high-voltage controller, which set HVIL alerts on an intact loop; the fix is a ferrite clipped around the thickest tan wire of that harness branch.",["Interference from another load coupling into the supply of the monitoring controller","Loose contact in a loop N connector","Ferrite or shielding missing after harness repair","Evaluation software of the controller too sensitive"],["High-voltage warning that appears briefly, sometimes when braking","No fault found on loop resistance checks","Occasional refusal to become ready"],3,3,["U353D","U353F","U3540","U353A","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ N — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U353F:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit N Low","U353F covers a loop N value under the permitted minimum. The defect can sit inside a consumer rather than in the harness. For the Cummins battery electric systems BES CM2450 EV110B and EV111B, bulletin TSB250044 ties fault codes 8174 (interlock level too low or grounded) and 8175 to the electric air compressor: once the interlock contacts of the HV cable to the compressor pass, the measurement moves to the interlock…",["Interlock path inside an HV consumer such as an electric air compressor open or high-resistance","HV cable plug on loop N not reconnected properly","Loop N wire shorted to ground"],["High voltage switches off and stays off","Interlock fault returns although all cable plugs test fine","Auxiliary drive such as the air compressor not running"],3,3,["U353D","U353E","U3540","U353B","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ N — ערך נמוך"],U3540:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit N High","U3540 reports loop N on the high side of its permitted window. In converted or repowered vehicles the installer often assembles the loop. The hardware manual of BorgWarner's Cascadia Motion CM inverters offers a pin pair, HVIL_IN and HVIL_OUT, that is bridged inside once every HV plug of the inverter is fitted, and leaves the safety of the whole installation to the installer.",["Extra contacts, splices or adapter harnesses from a conversion raise loop N resistance","Loop N wire shorted to a 12 V or 24 V feed","Poorly crimped or loose interlock terminal"],["No ready mode right after a conversion or component swap","High-voltage system warning","Charging blocked"],3,3,["U353D","U353E","U353F","U353C","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ N — ערך גבוה"],U3541:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit O","U3541 denotes trouble on interlock circuit O, the fourteenth loop. What happens next may depend on the operating state. Tesla's 2013 HVIL diagnostic guide for the Model S, published through NHTSA, splits the reaction: in the modes Standby, Support and Charge the battery management stores a fault and opens the contactors, or leaves them open if they already are, whereas in Drive it only raises a warning so that the…",["Connector in loop O not fully latched","Loop O wiring damaged","Internal fault in an HV component on loop O"],["Warning while driving without loss of drive","No ready mode after the vehicle was switched off","Charging refused"],3,3,["U3542","U3543","U3544","U353D","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ O"],U3542:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit O Performance","U3542 marks loop O as implausible. Interlock trouble often clusters around charging. Mercedes bulletin LI54.10-P-067823 for the third-generation smart electric drive with the optional 22 kW on-board charger, built before 25 March 2013, links sporadic or permanent interlock codes (P0A0A00, P0A0E00), a no-start with a charging-cable message and a battery that will not charge to loose low-voltage contacts at that…",["Loose low-voltage contact at the on-board charger carrying loop O","Contact that opens only when components are hot or cold","Internal fault in the on-board charger"],["Vehicle will not start and reports a plugged-in charging cable","Charging does not start or stops","Fault at the beginning or end of a charging session"],3,3,["U3541","U3543","U3544","U353E","P0A0B","P0A0E"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ O — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3543:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit O Low","With U3543, loop O has dropped under its minimum. Some plug designs let the fitter see the reason. An LG Electronics patent describes a high-voltage connector closed by turning a cover housing: the rotation moves an inner cap up or down so that the power terminals mate first and the shorter interlock tab last, while a scale on the plug housing shows how far the cover has turned.",["Rotary HV plug on loop O not turned to its end position","Interlock tab or socket in a loop O plug bent or pushed back","Loop O wire shorted to ground"],["High voltage stays off after work on HV plugs","No ready mode","Charging not possible"],3,3,["U3541","U3542","U3544","U353F","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ O — ערך נמוך"],U3544:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit O High","U3544 sets when loop O delivers too high a value. A plug can hold its specified torque and still sit crooked. FCA's STAR case S2108000121 (Rev. B, 2026) for Wrangler and Grand Cherokee 4xe models describes P0A0A after HV repairs although the connector bolts reached 9 Nm: the plug had gone on at an angle, the C3 connector of the power inverter module in particular.",["HV plug on loop O torqued down while tilted","Interlock terminals spread by a crooked fitting","Loop O wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Connector bolt thread stripped so the plug cannot be clamped"],["Check engine light and hybrid system message right after an HV repair","No ready mode"],3,3,["U3541","U3542","U3543","U3540","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ O — ערך גבוה"],U3545:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit P","U3545 is the general fault code for interlock circuit P, the fifteenth loop. Interlock electronics can be harmed by events elsewhere in the drive. Allison service letter SIL 3-EP-14 (Rev. C, 2017) for the H 40/50 EP hybrid system used in buses offers a separate HVIL circuit card for the DPIM2 inverter: if the check list shows 3 to 4 µF between DC+ or DC− and chassis, for example after an internal stator short, that…",["Interlock circuit board inside the inverter damaged, e.g. after a motor winding short","Connector in loop P not fully latched","Loop P wiring damaged","Electrostatic damage to monitoring electronics during service"],["Vehicle cannot be made ready","Other drive faults stored at the same time, such as motor or isolation faults"],4,3,["U3546","U3547","U3548","U3541","P0A0A"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ P"],U3546:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit P Performance","U3546 marks loop P as implausible. On large vehicles the mechanical routing of HV cables affects the interlock too. Gillig's field service campaign FSC 22-13-2479 for its Gen 2.0 and 2.5 battery electric buses found that HV battery cables in one equipment compartment lacked adequate support brackets;",["HV cable without adequate brackets pulling on a loop P plug","Loose contact in a loop P connector","Cable clamp or bracket not refitted after repair"],["Interlock fault that comes and goes, more often on rough roads","High-voltage warning lamp lighting briefly","Brief loss of high-voltage power"],3,3,["U3545","U3547","U3548","U3542","P0A0B"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ P — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3547:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit P Low","U3547 reports a low value on loop P, and the contactors drop out with it. A design flaw can be the cause too. Kenworth (campaign 25KWC) and Peterbilt (25PBC) recalled battery electric T680E, 520EV and 579EV trucks under NHTSA number 25V181: with certain HVIL circuit layouts in their Accelera power control accessory subsystem, high voltage could be lost and the contactors open without warning, cutting propulsion.",["Interlock circuit layout covered by a recall, overlay harness not yet fitted","Plug in loop P open or interlock pin pushed back","Loop P wire shorted to ground"],["Sudden loss of propulsion while driving","Contactors open without prior warning","No restart until the loop reads normal"],4,3,["U3545","U3546","U3548","U3543","P0A0C"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ P — ערך נמוך"],U3548:["High Voltage System Interlock Circuit P High","U3548 is the high-side code of loop P. When each unit adds a known share of loop resistance, a single suspect can be isolated by substitution. Tesla's Model S HVIL guide has technicians, after consulting a field engineer, place a 60-ohm resistor across the drive inverter's interlock pins at connector X250 and also bridge its CAN lines; if the contactors then close, the inverter's internal section is to blame.",["Internal interlock section of an HV component too resistive","Loop P wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Loose or poorly crimped interlock terminal in loop P"],["Contactors stay open, no ready mode","High-voltage system warning","Charging blocked"],3,3,["U3545","U3546","U3547","U3544","P0A0D"],"מעגל נעילת בטיחות מערכת מתח גבוה‏ P — ערך גבוה"],U3549:["Hydrogen Tank High Pressure Sensor 1 Circuit","U3549 covers the electrical circuit of the high-pressure sensor that reads hydrogen pressure on the storage side, upstream of the regulator, where a full system holds up to 70 MPa, the ceiling set by FMVSS 308.",["Corroded or damaged connector or wiring between sensor and storage controller","High-pressure sensor faulty internally","Sensor supply voltage or ground missing","Hydrogen storage control unit faulty"],["Hydrogen system warning in the instrument cluster","Fuel gauge or range display missing or implausible","Fuel cell power limited"],4,3,["U3564","U3565","U3552","U0119"],"חיישן לחץ גבוה מיכל מימן‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354A:["Hydrogen Tank A Temperature Sensor 1 Circuit","U354A reports an electrical fault on the first temperature sensor of hydrogen tank A. Tank sensors matter most while refuelling: compression heats the gas, and FMVSS 308 slows the pressure ramp once the gas inside passes 85 °C; on the Mirai the tank temperature is passed to the dispenser by infrared.",["Outdated software in the unit that evaluates the tank sensors","Temperature sensor inside the tank failed (often only as tank assembly)","Open or short in the sensor wiring or connector at the tank"],["Code sets while refuelling","Hydrogen system warning","Refuelling slower or ends before the tank is full"],4,1,["U354B","U354C","U354E","U3549"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ A 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354B:["Hydrogen Tank A Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","U354B is the circuit code for the second temperature sensor in tank A. One probe cannot capture a long tank during a fast fill: in tests published in the HySafe journal, sensors in on-tank valves at both ends of a Type IV tank finished a fill around 30 °C apart, and the authors concluded that even two positions miss the hottest zone.",["Wiring or connector fault at the far tank end","Second temperature sensor of tank A failed","Evaluation software misjudging the sensor pair"],["Tank cannot be filled completely","Hydrogen system warning"],4,1,["U354A","U354D","U354F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ A 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354C:["Hydrogen Tank B Temperature Sensor 1 Circuit","U354C flags the circuit of the first temperature sensor in tank B. The maker decides which tank is B, and every series fuel cell car has at least two: the first Mirai carried tanks of 60.0 and 62.4 litres, the Clarity a main and a sub tank. With several tanks the readings can be checked against each other.",["Open or short in the wiring to tank B","Temperature sensor 1 of tank B failed","Input stage of the storage control unit faulty"],["Hydrogen system warning","Refuelling limited or interrupted"],4,1,["U354D","U354A","U354E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ B 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354D:["Hydrogen Tank B Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","U354D marks an electrical fault on the second temperature sensor of tank B. Apart from fill control, tank temperature is needed to convert pressure into fuel quantity, because cold gas at a given pressure holds more hydrogen than warm gas. Sensors and wiring sit at the tank under the floor, often inside the on-tank valve.",["Moisture or damage at the underbody connector of tank B","Temperature sensor 2 of tank B failed","Harness chafed after underbody or tank work"],["Hydrogen system warning","Fuel gauge less accurate","Refuelling ends early"],4,1,["U354C","U354B","U354F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ B 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354E:["Hydrogen Tank C Temperature Sensor 1 Circuit","U354E points to an electrical fault on sensor 1 of tank C, a tank that exists only on three-tank vehicles: the second-generation Mirai, whose long central tank is joined by two smaller ones crosswise under the rear seat and the boot, or the Nexo with three tanks holding 156 litres. On a two-tank car such as the first Mirai or the Clarity the code would suggest a configuration or software mismatch.",["Wiring or connector fault at tank C","Temperature sensor 1 of tank C failed","Controller coded for a different number of tanks"],["Hydrogen system warning","Refuelling slower or stopped early"],4,1,["U354F","U354A","U354C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ C 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U354F:["Hydrogen Tank C Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","U354F is set when the circuit of the second temperature sensor in tank C fails. During refuelling the car hands tank data to the station; Toyota describes infrared links between the tank temperature sensors, nozzle and dispenser that set the flow so the gas does not overheat.",["Open or short in the wiring of sensor 2 at tank C","Temperature sensor 2 of tank C failed","Evaluation software needing a manufacturer update"],["Refuelling takes longer or stops before full","Hydrogen system warning","Reduced range after refuelling"],4,1,["U354E","U354B","U354D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל מימן‏ C 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3550:["Hydrogen Tank A Valve Control Circuit","U3550 indicates an electrical fault in the control circuit of the solenoid valve on hydrogen tank A. This on-tank valve is the primary closure between tank and fuel system, and FMVSS 308 requires it to default to closed when unpowered.",["Wiring or connector fault between controller and valve","Solenoid coil of the tank A valve open or shorted","Valve driver stage in the storage control unit faulty"],["Hydrogen system warning","Reduced range, or no READY if the car depends on this tank"],4,3,["U3551","U3552","U3553","U3556"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ A — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],U3551:["Hydrogen Tank A Valve Enable Circuit","U3551 concerns the enable circuit of the valve on tank A: not the switched control line, but the path that permits the valve to be powered at all, typically a relay, fuse or supply-side switch. Designs keep it apart so a crash can cut hydrogen reliably.",["Enable or crash cutoff relay faulty","Blown fuse or missing supply in the valve enable path","Open or short in the enable wiring to valve A"],["No READY or fuel cell does not start","Hydrogen system warning"],4,3,["U3550","U3552","U3554","U3557"],"אפשור שסתום מיכל מימן‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3552:["Hydrogen Tank A Valve Performance","U3552 is the performance code for the valve on tank A: the circuit tests good, but the valve does not act as commanded, either staying shut or failing to seal. With several tanks this is hard to see, because one pressure sensor where the tank lines merge cannot tell that a single tank no longer delivers.",["Tank A valve stuck closed or opening sluggishly","Valve seat no longer sealing","Implausible tank pressure reading misleading the check"],["Noticeably lower range than the gauge suggests","Hydrogen system warning"],4,3,["U3550","U3551","U3555","U3558"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3553:["Hydrogen Tank B Valve Control Circuit","U3553 means the controller sees a fault in the drive circuit of the solenoid valve on tank B, such as an open coil, a short to ground or supply, or an output that does not follow its command. Hyundai shows in a patent how such valves can be checked: one current sensor reads the operating current of several tank solenoids;",["Damaged wiring or corroded connector to the tank B valve","Solenoid coil open or shorted","Output stage of the control unit faulty"],["Hydrogen system warning","Range reduced because tank B is not used"],4,3,["U3554","U3555","U3550","U3556"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ B — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],U3554:["Hydrogen Tank B Valve Enable Circuit","U3554 refers to the enable path that powers the tank B solenoid. Its purpose is a second, independent way to withdraw the permission for the valve to open. Toyota patented a layout in which the valve controller and the controller for high voltage sit at opposite ends of the car and back each other up: after a crash at one end, the controller at the undamaged end shuts the hydrogen valve.",["Enable relay or switch in the supply path faulty","Open or short in the enable line to valve B","Faulty input that withdraws the release, such as a crash or flap signal"],["Hydrogen system warning","Range reduced or no READY"],4,3,["U3553","U3555","U3551","U3557"],"אפשור שסתום מיכל מימן‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3555:["Hydrogen Tank B Valve Performance","U3555 reports that the valve on tank B does not behave as expected although its circuit tests good. Leakage through the closed valve is one form. Hyundai patented a check for it while the car is parked: at wake-ups, hydrogen left in the supply line is fed into the stack with the tank valves shut, so the high-pressure reading should fall slightly;",["Tank B valve seat leaking when closed","Valve not opening mechanically","Manual tank valve not reopened after service"],["Hydrogen system warning, sometimes after parking","Range lower than expected"],4,3,["U3553","U3554","U3552","U3558"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],U3556:["Hydrogen Tank C Valve Control Circuit","U3556 is the control circuit code for the valve on tank C, the third tank found only on three-tank layouts such as the Nexo or the current Mirai. On the Mirai the two crosswise tanks behind the long central one are the smaller ones, so losing one costs only part of the range. That makes the fault easy to overlook while driving.",["Wiring or connector fault at the tank C valve","Valve coil open or shorted","Driver stage for valve C faulty"],["Hydrogen system warning","Range noticeably shorter after a full fill"],4,3,["U3557","U3558","U3550","U3553"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ C — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],U3557:["Hydrogen Tank C Valve Enable Circuit","U3557 is stored for a fault in the enable circuit of the tank C valve, the third tank of three-tank vehicles. Permission to open is not tied to driving alone: a Honda patent describes the cutoff valve being open with the ignition off, for example when the stack keeps operating after shutdown, so collision detection stays powered in that state and a cutoff relay can still close the valve.",["Cutoff or enable relay for valve C faulty","Fuse or common valve supply interrupted","Enable line to tank C damaged"],["Hydrogen system warning, possibly right after switch-off or at start","Reduced range"],4,3,["U3556","U3558","U3551","U3554"],"אפשור שסתום מיכל מימן‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3558:["Hydrogen Tank C Valve","U3558 is listed only as Hydrogen Tank C Valve, without a fault type, so it serves as the general valve code for tank C on three-tank vehicles. FMVSS 308 shows what such a valve must withstand: tens of thousands of pressure cycles, partly at extreme temperatures, chatter flow, and afterwards no more than 10 NmL of leakage per hour.",["Tank C valve sticking or not sealing","Electrical fault at the valve without its own circuit code","Tank and valve beyond their service life"],["Hydrogen system warning","Shorter range"],4,3,["U3556","U3557","U3552","U3555"],"שסתום מיכל מימן‏ C"],U3559:["Air Inlet Pressure Sensor Circuit","U3559 flags a wiring or signal fault on the first pressure sensor of the air supply that feeds the stack, located behind the air filter and ahead of the electric compressor. Its reading is the suction pressure of the compressor: in a Toyota patent the delivery pressure is divided by it to place the operating point on the compressor map and keep clear of the surge line, and Nissan derives the compressor inlet…",["Connector or wiring at the air filter housing wet, corroded or damaged","Inlet pressure sensor faulty internally","5 V supply or ground of the sensor missing","Fuel cell control unit faulty or needing a software update"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, especially under high load or at altitude","Unusual compressor noise"],4,3,["U355A","U355B","U355C","U3561"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת אוויר — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U355A:["Charge Air Cooler Outlet Pressure Sensor 1 Circuit","U355A concerns the first of two pressure sensors behind the charge air cooler, where compressed and cooled air heads for the humidifier and the stack. This is the pressure the system really regulates: in a Nissan patent a sensor between intercooler and water recovery unit is the feedback for compressor torque and the outlet pressure valve, and the controller caps this pressure so that compressor and humidifier stay…",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of sensor 1","Pressure sensor 1 faulty internally","Shared 5 V supply or ground faulty (often with other sensor codes)"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Noticeably reduced power","Compressor speed fluctuates or stays high"],4,3,["U355B","U355C","U3559","U355F"],"חיישן לחץ יציאת מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U355B:["Charge Air Cooler Outlet Pressure Sensor 2 Circuit","U355B points to a circuit problem with pressure sensor 2 at the charge air cooler outlet. J2012 lists two at this spot, which points to a pair used for cross-checking; how a maker splits the roles is unpublished, and no public document uses U355B.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of sensor 2","Condensed water frozen on the sensor (occurs at cold start, may clear when warm)","Pressure sensor 2 faulty internally"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Start refused or system shuts down shortly after a cold start","Reduced power while only one pressure sensor is valid"],4,3,["U355A","U355C","U3559"],"חיישן לחץ יציאת מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U355C:["Charge Air Cooler Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit","U355C reports a circuit fault on the temperature sensor behind the charge air cooler. Compression heats the air strongly: Honda gives about 120 °C at the compressor outlet, while the stack works at 80 to 90 °C, so the air is first brought down to roughly 60 to 75 °C. The sensor confirms this cooling before the air reaches the humidifier.",["Open or short in wiring or connector of the temperature sensor","Temperature sensor (thermistor) faulty internally","Sensor ground or reference circuit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Power limited, especially under sustained high load","Compressor runs at reduced speed"],4,3,["U355A","U355B","U3559"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U355D:["Expander Inlet Pressure Sensor 1 Circuit","U355D covers the first pressure sensor in front of the expander, a turbine in the cathode exhaust that turns leftover pressure from the stack outlet into shaft power for the compressor. Garrett states that its optional turbine expander, developed among others for the compressor of the BMW iX5 Hydrogen, lowers the electricity needed for compression by up to 20 %.",["Wiring or connector of sensor 1 at the wet exhaust side corroded, open or shorted","Expander inlet pressure sensor 1 faulty internally","Sensor supply or ground faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Higher hydrogen consumption because less energy is recovered","Reduced peak power"],4,3,["U355E","U355F","U3560","U3559"],""],U355E:["Expander Inlet Pressure Sensor 2 Circuit","U355E names a circuit fault on pressure sensor 2 at the expander inlet. Conditions there are harsh: cathode exhaust carries the product water of the stack, and Volkswagen notes in a turbine patent that the pressure drop inside the turbine makes water condense even behind a droplet separator, eroding the blades.",["Wiring or connector of sensor 2 corroded by exhaust moisture, open or shorted","Water frozen in the sensor port at cold start","Expander inlet pressure sensor 2 faulty internally"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Fault appears mainly after cold starts","Reduced power if sensor 1 is affected as well"],4,3,["U355D","U355F","U3560","U3562"],""],U355F:["Cathode Backpressure Valve Control Circuit","U355F reports a wiring or output stage fault on the actuator of the valve at the cathode outlet, which throttles the air leaving the stack and thereby sets the pressure the air side runs at. GM moves such a valve in closed loop on a pressure reading, in steps or continuously. U355F itself is absent from public maker documents.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the valve actuator (wet exhaust area)","Valve motor or actuator winding faulty","Driver stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty or software outdated"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Noticeably reduced power","Fuel cell system shuts down or vehicle does not reach READY"],4,3,["U3560","U3561","U3562","U355D"],""],U3560:["Cathode Backpressure Valve Position Sensor Circuit","U3560 is set when the signal of the position sensor on the cathode backpressure valve is missing, shorted or outside its electrical range. Outlet valves of this kind are often throttle flaps whose angle is reported back, as a Hydrogenics patent shows for the cathode and purge valves of a stack.",["Open, short or moisture in the position sensor wiring or connector","Position sensor faulty (often only available with the valve unit)","Sensor 5 V supply or ground missing"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power","Further air path codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["U355F","U3563","U3561","U355D"],""],U3561:["Cathode Bypass Valve Control Circuit","U3561 points to a break, a short or an output stage fault in the actuator circuit of the cathode bypass valve. This valve lets part of the compressor delivery skip the stack and flow straight into the exhaust. Nissan gives two reasons: keeping the compressor clear of surge when the stack needs little air, and putting enough air into the exhaust to dilute the hydrogen released when the anode is purged.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the bypass valve","Bypass valve motor or actuator faulty","Driver stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, compressor speed fluctuating at low load","Fuel cell system does not start"],4,3,["U3562","U3563","U355F","U3559"],""],U3562:["Cathode Bypass Valve","Unlike U3561, this code concerns how the cathode bypass valve itself behaves: it does not reach or hold the opening the controller asks for, for instance because it sticks. A Toyota patent shows why a valve stuck shut is serious. While a cold stack is warmed by deliberately inefficient generation, bypass air is supposed to thin out hydrogen in the exhaust;",["Valve frozen in place after a cold soak","Valve sticking from deposits or wear","Actuator too weak or gear damaged","Position feedback reading wrong, valve itself fine"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power or failed start in frost","Unusual compressor or air noise"],4,3,["U3561","U3563","U355F","U3559"],""],U3563:["Cathode Bypass Valve Position Sensor Circuit","U3563 means the position sensor on the cathode bypass valve delivers no usable signal because of a broken wire, a short or a voltage outside its window. Toyota's patent mounts such a valve body position sensor right at the bypass valve, with pressure sensors before and after it; the angle tells the controller how the compressor air is really being split between stack and bypass.",["Open, short or moisture in the position sensor wiring or connector","Position sensor in the valve unit faulty","Shared 5 V supply or ground faulty (often with other sensor codes)"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, especially at low load"],4,3,["U3561","U3562","U3560","U355F"],""],U3564:["Hydrogen Supply Line A Pressure Sensor 1 Circuit","U3564 deals with the wiring of pressure sensor 1 on hydrogen supply line A, most likely the medium-pressure section behind the tank regulator; J2012 does not fix the spot. Toyota's patent shows such a layout: a mechanical reducing valve brings tank hydrogen down to roughly 1.1–1.6 MPa, an intermediate pressure sensor watches that section, and the injector then lowers the pressure to about 200–300 kPa for the stack.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of pressure sensor 1","Pressure sensor 1 faulty internally (maker may supply a revised part)","5 V supply or ground of the sensor missing","Fuel cell control unit faulty or needing a software update"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power","Fuel cell system may refuse to start"],4,3,["U3565","U3549","U3566","U3550"],"חיישן לחץ קו אספקת מימן‏ A 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3565:["Hydrogen Supply Line A Pressure Sensor 2 Circuit","U3565 signals that the second pressure sensor of hydrogen supply line A has a wiring problem. Two sensors on one line let the controller cross-check them, and Hyundai's Nexo shows how such a pair is handled in service: when hydrogen pressure sensor 1 or 2 (P315200, P315300) set codes, campaign T4E from 2019 had both swapped for a revised part at an outdoor venting spot, followed by an offset reset and a leak test;",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of pressure sensor 2","Pressure sensor 2 faulty internally","Sensor membrane damaged during a previous repair","Fuel cell control unit faulty or needing a software update"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Often no noticeable change while sensor 1 still works","Reduced power"],4,3,["U3564","U3567","U3566","U3549"],"חיישן לחץ קו אספקת מימן‏ A 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3566:["Anode Inlet Pressure Sensor 1 Circuit","U3566 is set for an electrical fault at anode inlet pressure sensor 1, sitting between hydrogen injector and stack. A GM patent explains why this value is central: it closes the loop for the injector and also feeds anode valve control and the handling of hydrogen in the exhaust. A wrong value derails that loop;",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of sensor 1 at the stack","Anode inlet pressure sensor 1 faulty internally","Shared 5 V supply or ground faulty (often with other sensor codes)"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Noticeably reduced power","Rough or interrupted fuel cell start"],4,3,["U3567","U3564","U3576","U3568"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת אנודה‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3567:["Anode Inlet Pressure Sensor 2 Circuit","U3567 belongs to the second pressure sensor at the anode inlet. Its signal carries safety weight: GM uses anode pressure to catch an injector stuck open, then shuts the tank valves, opens the anode bleed valve, lifts cathode pressure with compressor and backpressure valve and opens the cathode bypass so hydrogen in the exhaust stays diluted.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of sensor 2 at the stack","Anode inlet pressure sensor 2 faulty internally","Water in the connector, fault mainly after frost"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Often no noticeable change while sensor 1 still works","Reduced power"],4,3,["U3566","U3565","U3576","U3568"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת אנודה‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3568:["Anode Multifunction Valve Control Circuit","U3568 flags trouble in the electrical drive of the anode multifunction valve: an open wire, a short against ground or battery voltage, or a failed output stage. The code title does not say which duties the valve combines; known designs merge draining water and purging nitrogen in one solenoid below the anode water separator.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the valve (wet area below the stack)","Solenoid coil of the valve open or shorted","Driver stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Power dropping off the longer the drive lasts","Fuel cell system shuts down or does not start"],4,3,["U3569","U356A","U356C","U3566"],""],U3569:["Anode Multifunction Valve","With U3569 the multifunction valve can be driven but does not do what it is told: it stays shut, leaks or reacts too slowly. A solenoid of this kind usually lacks position feedback, so its state is inferred.",["Valve frozen shut after parking in frost","Valve sticking or leaking from deposits or worn seat","Water level sensor of the separator reads wrong, valve itself fine","Control software needs an update"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, uneven fuel cell output","Start refused or shutdown, mainly after frost","Higher hydrogen consumption"],4,3,["U3568","U356B","U356D","U3567"],""],U356A:["Anode Drain Valve Control Circuit","U356A concerns the electrical drive of the solenoid sitting under the anode water trap, which lets condensate leave the hydrogen loop. Hyundai opens it when a level sensor reports a full trap and closes it at a low mark so no hydrogen follows; if that sensor fails, the valve is closed as soon as anode pressure falls faster than a set rate.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the drain valve","Drain valve solenoid coil open or shorted","Driver stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power after some driving time","Fuel cell system shuts down"],4,3,["U356B","U356C","U356E","U3568"],"שסתום ניקוז אנודה — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],U356B:["Anode Drain Valve","U356B is about how the drain valve behaves, not its wiring. Hyundai shows how such faults are separated: if the level in the trap fails to drop within a set time after an open command while the position sensor still reports closed, the valve is judged stuck shut; the system then limits current, drains on a schedule derived from accumulated charge and runs the stack warmer so water leaves as vapour.",["Drain valve frozen after parking in frost","Valve sticking or not sealing due to deposits or a worn seat","Water level sensor of the trap faulty, valve itself fine","Drain line downstream of the valve blocked or iced"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Power limited, fuel cell running hotter than usual","System shutdown if the valve stays open"],4,3,["U356A","U356D","U356E","U3569"],"שסתום ניקוז אנודה"],U356C:["Anode Header Drain Valve Control Circuit","U356C covers the drive circuit of a second drain valve mounted directly on the anode exhaust header, the channel inside the stack that gathers the gas leaving every cell. GM lists three valves behind the stack: a bleed valve at the top of the anode sump, a drain valve at its bottom and this header valve, which empties into the cathode exhaust.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the header drain valve","Valve solenoid coil open or shorted","Driver stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Power limited, especially after parking on a slope","Often no noticeable effect at first"],4,3,["U356D","U356A","U356F","U3568"],""],U356D:["Anode Header Drain Valve","U356D is set when the header drain valve responds electrically yet does not empty the header as intended. GM splits each opening into two phases: first water runs out of the header, then nitrogen-rich gas is bled off. The end of the water phase is recognised from stack voltage or from an estimated gas flow across the valve, and the bleed phase is sized by the hydrogen content of the anode.",["Header drain valve or its line frozen","Valve sticking or leaking from deposits or a worn seat","Header drain line to the cathode exhaust blocked"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, uneven cell voltages","Higher hydrogen consumption if the valve stays open"],4,3,["U356C","U356B","U356F","U3576"],""],U356E:["Anode Drain Valve Heater Relay Control Circuit","U356E refers to the relay that powers the heater on the anode drain valve, more precisely to its coil drive from the fuel cell controller. Drain valves sit in the wettest corner of the hydrogen loop and can freeze shut after a cold night. Hyundai fits PTC heaters to its purge valves, fed by the battery and switched on when a start below freezing is detected;",["Open, short or corrosion in the relay coil wiring or connector","Heater relay faulty","Fuse or supply of the relay circuit missing","Relay driver in the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell warning message","Delayed or failed start in frost","Often no noticeable effect in warm weather"],2,0,["U356F","U356A","U356B"],"ממסר גוף חימום שסתום ניקוז אנודה — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],U356F:["Anode Header Drain Valve Heater Relay Control Circuit","U356F reports that the relay feeding the heater on the anode header drain valve cannot be driven properly because its coil circuit is open or shorted. That valve hangs on the stack's anode outlet header, where condensate gathers and can freeze during a cold soak. GM targets exactly this zone with heated outlet manifolds so ice does not block them during subzero starts.",["Open, short or corrosion in the relay coil wiring or connector","Heater relay faulty","Relay driver in the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell warning message","Start problems after a frosty night","Battery discharged if the heater stays on"],2,0,["U356E","U356C","U356D"],""],U3570:["Stack Inlet Coolant Temperature Sensor Circuit","U3570 signals that the sensor for coolant entering the stack sends a broken, shorted or out-of-range reading. Thermal control is steered by this value: Hyundai describes a three-port valve which gets the stack inlet temperature from the fuel cell control unit over CAN and sets its opening from it, and in a Nissan patent the current drawn from the stack is capped once inlet coolant passes a set point, so that the…",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the inlet sensor","Inlet coolant temperature sensor faulty internally (drift, internal open)","Coolant seeping past the sensor seal into the connector","Input stage of the fuel cell control unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power, especially under high load","Implausible stack inlet temperature in live data"],3,3,["U3571","U3572","U3573","U3574"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור כניסת מצבור תאי דלק — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3571:["Stack Outlet Coolant Temperature Sensor 1 Circuit","U3571 concerns the wiring and signal of sensor 1 in the coolant stream leaving the stack. Coolant is hottest here, so the reading serves as the main overheat guard: GM holds stack outlet temperature mainly with a three-port valve sending coolant past or through the radiator and shuts the stack off when coolant at this point gets too hot.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of outlet sensor 1","Outlet temperature sensor 1 faulty internally or drifting","Connector or wiring near the hot outlet line damaged by heat"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Power reduced or fuel cell system switched off as a precaution","Outlet temperatures of sensor 1 and sensor 2 disagree in live data"],3,3,["U3572","U3570","U3574"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור יציאת מצבור תאי דלק‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3572:["Stack Outlet Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","U3572 is logged when the second coolant temperature sensor at the stack outlet has a wiring or signal problem. No maker explains in public why two sensors share this spot; mutual checking is the obvious reason.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of outlet sensor 2","Outlet temperature sensor 2 faulty internally","Shared sensor ground faulty (often with U3571 at the same time)"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Little or no change in driving as long as sensor 1 is valid","Reduced power if both outlet sensors are affected"],3,3,["U3571","U3570","U3574"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור יציאת מצבור תאי דלק‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],U3573:["Coolant Mixing Valve Control Circuit","U3573 concerns how the coolant mixing valve is powered: its actuator line may be interrupted or shorted, or the output stage may have failed. This three-way valve splits stack coolant between radiator and bypass and so decides how warm it is when it returns to the stack.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the valve actuator","Actuator motor or solenoid coil of the mixing valve faulty","Driver stage or CAN link of the controlling unit faulty"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Stack temperature too high or too low, reduced power","Slow warm-up of the fuel cell system"],3,3,["U3574","U3575","U3570"],""],U3574:["Coolant Mixing Valve","U3574 serves as the catch-all for the coolant mixing valve when the trouble lies in its behaviour rather than its wiring: it sticks, moves too slowly or misses the commanded split between radiator and bypass. Temperatures reveal it, because GM sets stack outlet temperature with this valve and the inlet-to-outlet difference with pump speed, so a jammed valve upsets both.",["Valve element sticking from deposits, worn seal or unsuitable coolant","Actuator gear or motor worn, valve moves sluggishly","Internal leak, coolant passes the closed port","Air in the stack coolant loop after service distorting the temperature response"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Stack temperature swings or stays too high under load","Reduced power, slow warm-up in cold weather"],3,3,["U3573","U3575","U3570","U3571"],""],U3575:["Coolant Mixing Valve Position Sensor Circuit","U3575 deals with wiring and signal of the sensor reporting how far the coolant mixing valve is open. GM lists feedback of the valve position, next to two temperature sensors, among the parts its stack outlet temperature control relies on. In Toyota's design the sensor is built into the valve and returns the angle of the valving element;",["Open, short or moisture in the position sensor wiring or connector","Position sensor faulty (usually replaced together with the valve)","Sensor supply or ground missing"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Stack temperature regulated less precisely, reduced power","Valve opening shown as invalid in live data"],3,3,["U3573","U3574","U3570"],""],U3576:["Stack Differential Pressure Sensor Circuit","U3576 is set when the stack differential pressure sensor delivers no signal, a shorted one or one outside its valid range. The title leaves open which two pressures it compares. In a GM patent such a sensor is plumbed between anode and cathode side, as the anode is normally kept slightly above the cathode.",["Open, short or corrosion in wiring or connector of the differential pressure sensor","Water or ice in the sensor ports or a failed sensor heater","Differential pressure sensor faulty internally"],["Fuel cell system warning, MIL on","Reduced power or fuel cell system shuts down","No start, especially after a cold night"],3,3,["U3566","U3567","U356D"],"חיישן לחץ דיפרנציאל מצבור תאי דלק — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"]};export{e as default};
